21cb9b4b1b9a5b281d441809371010b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:04:59Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:04:59Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"message":"feat(recorder): renderer chip input for meeting speech-context terms (#1024 slice 4)\n\nThe meeting planner now lets the user TYPE the meeting''s speech-context\nvocabulary. A tag/chip input (SpeechContextTermsInput) collects terms, shows\neach normalized chip (the exact string that will persist), and enforces the\nsame <=32 term / <=64 char caps the contract applies. Terms flow\nMeetingPlanner.onSubmit -> handleCreateMeetingContract -> meeting.createContract,\nwhere the main process (slice 3) re-normalizes and merges them ahead of the\nrecorder''s per-session terms before Speechmatics additional_vocab, biasing live\ntranscription for every recording of the meeting.\n\nWHERE: the planner is the existing meeting-setup form (title/description/\nschedule/provider), so term entry is a field-add there -- no new screen, no\nper-session dialog. The existing per-session \"Sozluk\" textarea is untouched.\n\n- src/audio/speech-context-terms.ts: renderer-safe pure mirror of the main\n  process normalizeSpeechContextTerms (NFKC, whitespace collapse, case-sensitive\n  exact dedupe, drop blank/oversized, cap 32) + consts. A drift-guard test pins\n  the same canonical case the meeting-client test asserts (renderer cannot import\n  the Node-only main-process module).\n- src/components/SpeechContextTermsInput.tsx: controlled chip input -- Enter/comma\n  commits, Backspace removes the last chip, x removes a specific chip, paste\n  splits on newline/comma, blur commits a pending draft; duplicate/too-long/cap\n  hints; N/32 counter.\n- MeetingPlan gains speechContextTerms; App threads plan.speechContextTerms into\n  createContract (omitted when empty -> byte-identical term-less contract).\n- electron/preload.ts exposes speechContextTerms on the createContract payload\n  type (the IPC handler already parsed it in slice 3).\n\nTests: speech-context-terms +6, SpeechContextTermsInput +10, MeetingPlanner +1\n(plus empty-default pin). vitest 55 files / 652 tests; typecheck + lint +\nformat:check + security:audit (0 vulns) + build all green. Browser smoke: verified\nlive in Chromium via a throwaway Vite preview (normalize, case-distinct dedupe,\nduplicate hint, chip remove, submit payload carries the terms; console clean).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2a2222f75ffa8a7d93fe62e94c9cd6df8986705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/a2a2222f75ffa8a7d93fe62e94c9cd6df8986705"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/337c8d5621cb9b4b1b9a5b281d441809371010b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/337c8d5621cb9b4b1b9a5b281d441809371010b0","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKDMzN2M4ZDU2MjFjYjliNGIxYjlhNWIyODFkNDQxODA5MzcxMDEwYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/36de75be3ab80cf69f6c536df627764aad69d756","sha":"36de75be3ab80cf69f6c536df627764aad69d756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/36de75be3ab80cf69f6c536df627764aad69d756"}],"sha":"337c8d5621cb9b4b1b9a5b281d441809371010b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/337c8d5621cb9b4b1b9a5b281d441809371010b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/36de75be3ab80cf69f6c536df627764aad69d756/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:09:58Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:09:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(recorder): carry consent-bound speechContextTerms on meeting create (#1024 dilim 3) (#129)\n\n* feat(recorder): carry consent-bound speechContextTerms on meeting create (#1024 slice 3)\n\nThe desktop recorder can now set the meeting''s speech-context vocabulary when it\ncreates the canonical meeting contract. CreateMeetingContractArgs gains\nspeechContextTerms; createMeetingContract normalizes them (NFKC, whitespace\ncollapse, case-sensitive exact dedupe, drop blank/oversized, cap 32) and includes\nthem in the POST body only when a usable term remains (term-less recordings keep\na byte-identical contract). The meeting:create-contract IPC handler parses the\narray through the boundary (wire-type + <=64 raw-entry ceiling; client does the\nsemantic normalization).\n\nThe audio gateway already merges these meeting-contract terms ahead of the\nrecorder''s own session terms before Speechmatics additional_vocab\n(platform-backend#1024 slice 2), so setting them here biases live transcription\nfor every recording of the meeting — no per-session term entry required.\n\nTests: meeting-client +3 (body echo with dedupe/trim, omit-when-empty, cap-32\nunit), ipc/meeting +2 (forward parsed terms, reject non-string-array). vitest\n36/36; tsc (app + electron projects) clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): override fast-uri to ^3.1.7 (GHSA-5jgf-p345-68v8 et al.)\n\nnpm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high (the CI security:audit gate) flags\nfast-uri 3.1.5 — pulled through ajv via electron-store (runtime) and\nelectron-builder — for four high-severity advisories: host confusion via\nskipped IDN canonicalization, SSRF via malformed IPv6 normalization, SSRF via\nrepeated hostname percent-decoding, and host confusion via percent-encoded\nscheme normalization. Pin the override to the patched ^3.1.7 (ajv accepts it).\nPre-existing and repo-wide (surfaced once the advisory published); folded here\nbecause it blocks this PR''s build gate. Verified: npm audit --omit=dev\n--audit-level=high → 0 vulnerabilities; recorder tests 36/36.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(recorder): prettier-format meeting ipc test (#1024 slice 3)\n\nCI format:check (prettier --check .) flagged electron/ipc/meeting.test.ts.\nFormatting only; no test logic change. Security audit + typecheck + lint +\nrecorder unit tests (36/36) all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d087ed5ab06b93295ca8cefefdeeb4e4965ebf31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/d087ed5ab06b93295ca8cefefdeeb4e4965ebf31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/36de75be3ab80cf69f6c536df627764aad69d756","verification":{"payload":"tree d087ed5ab06b93295ca8cefefdeeb4e4965ebf31\nparent 1a3b1947703f3143280df84ee757d7b724c7e892\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1788505798 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788505798 +0300\n\nfeat(recorder): carry consent-bound speechContextTerms on meeting create (#1024 dilim 3) (#129)\n\n* feat(recorder): carry consent-bound speechContextTerms on meeting create (#1024 slice 3)\n\nThe desktop recorder can now set the meeting''s speech-context vocabulary when it\ncreates the canonical meeting contract. CreateMeetingContractArgs gains\nspeechContextTerms; createMeetingContract normalizes them (NFKC, whitespace\ncollapse, case-sensitive exact dedupe, drop blank/oversized, cap 32) and includes\nthem in the POST body only when a usable term remains (term-less recordings keep\na byte-identical contract). The meeting:create-contract IPC handler parses the\narray through the boundary (wire-type + <=64 raw-entry ceiling; client does the\nsemantic normalization).\n\nThe audio gateway already merges these meeting-contract terms ahead of the\nrecorder''s own session terms before Speechmatics additional_vocab\n(platform-backend#1024 slice 2), so setting them here biases live transcription\nfor every recording of the meeting — no per-session term entry required.\n\nTests: meeting-client +3 (body echo with dedupe/trim, omit-when-empty, cap-32\nunit), ipc/meeting +2 (forward parsed terms, reject non-string-array). vitest\n36/36; tsc (app + electron projects) clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): override fast-uri to ^3.1.7 (GHSA-5jgf-p345-68v8 et al.)\n\nnpm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high (the CI security:audit gate) flags\nfast-uri 3.1.5 — pulled through ajv via electron-store (runtime) and\nelectron-builder — for four high-severity advisories: host confusion via\nskipped IDN canonicalization, SSRF via malformed IPv6 normalization, SSRF via\nrepeated hostname percent-decoding, and host confusion via percent-encoded\nscheme normalization. Pin the override to the patched ^3.1.7 (ajv accepts it).\nPre-existing and repo-wide (surfaced once the advisory published); folded here\nbecause it blocks this PR''s build gate. Verified: npm audit --omit=dev\n--audit-level=high → 0 vulnerabilities; recorder tests 36/36.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(recorder): prettier-format meeting ipc test (#1024 slice 3)\n\nCI format:check (prettier --check .) flagged electron/ipc/meeting.test.ts.\nFormatting only; no test logic change. Security audit + typecheck + lint +\nrecorder unit tests (36/36) all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmm7GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1UAQAKr0cmbo5eV0Am0nFACwPewi\nkzwj2sMmJSZI4GOnEC09gzAARSRKm74ooiWNPF5IYL44w5+UVTAEaPv3GVbl7cfW\nj4WfhCcc7UoGzIrFCGttNAy0ntf1h5gxu5w77UEd3SMzCR7kCcqEUFEnY4LBgrMP\n+az24vRcRE23RFenXSv+Gem5lThus5W3QNQmcdUsxexnsgR9hFj6xNzV0nACMidm\nbNlTQSNnIvP/gsOOvPhW5rPfZ6YRRQzEHcXcgbEvRb0Dk3s4OUOb9tMLdaIxqkUx\n7Jl7JWSwMzeF55xYMR4TpQgt+aGQI/J8D4vj0Ez6WejLCYEeKyrAIoCjGHE9LaNe\nmmAGHs9gMgjUlrAYJsLvLybgGtU4xC/aywL1/UBshasPB3JVoGGoItyMDSquXGkd\neX2XJRZqzOT1kYOhbrMxwaypHZalznHhEIpD1