i.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/82fdc2d6333713d2fa1174891d897eeaf40ebdc2"}],"sha":"5098b5dda9fff57a8749352d5963c53002d33d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/5098b5dda9fff57a8749352d5963c53002d33d0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/82fdc2d6333713d2fa1174891d897eeaf40ebdc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:30:31Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:30:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(transcript): typewriter reveal for the live tail (#120)\n\nField report 3 (gitops#3419): with the live WS lane finally active,\npartials still LAND in 2-4 word packets (network + Speechmatics partial\ncadence), and painting each packet at once reads as ''toplu yazıyor'' —\nthe instant-perception competitors achieve is a RENDER technique, not\njust transport cadence.\n\nThe tail now chases its target through advanceTypewriter on a 30ms\ntick: steady typing at one char per tick, accelerating via\ntypewriterBudget (up to 12 chars/tick) when backlog grows so the display\nnever falls behind the speaker; a revised partial snaps back to the\ncommon prefix instantly so a wrong hypothesis never lingers; an empty\ntarget (final swallowed the tail) clears immediately. Same-value state\nupdates are skipped by React, so the idle interval is free.\n\nTests: 7 typewriter unit cases; panel fluent test advances fake timers;\nrow-domain tests switch to the Satırlar view explicitly. 615/615,\ntypecheck + eslint + prettier clean.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e26ebf6c604e07be5c753e41c106d15660101a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/6e26ebf6c604e07be5c753e41c106d15660101a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/82fdc2d6333713d2fa1174891d897eeaf40ebdc2","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e26ebf6c604e07be5c753e41c106d15660101a6\nparent 12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785745831 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785745831 +0300\n\nfeat(transcript): typewriter reveal for the live tail (#120)\n\nField report 3 (gitops#3419): with the live WS lane finally active,\npartials still LAND in 2-4 word packets (network + Speechmatics partial\ncadence), and painting each packet at once reads as ''toplu yazıyor'' —\nthe instant-perception competitors achieve is a RENDER technique, not\njust transport cadence.\n\nThe tail now chases its target through advanceTypewriter on a 30ms\ntick: steady typing at one char per tick, accelerating via\ntypewriterBudget (up to 12 chars/tick) when backlog grows so the display\nnever falls behind the speaker; a revised partial snaps back to the\ncommon prefix instantly so a wrong hypothesis never lingers; an empty\ntarget (final swallowed the tail) clears immediately. Same-value state\nupdates are skipped by React, so the idle interval is free.\n\nTests: 7 typewriter unit cases; panel fluent test advances fake timers;\nrow-domain tests switch to the Satırlar view explicitly. 615/615,\ntypecheck + eslint + prettier clean.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcFGnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA38QAHOC2ZzhuRWQbNCwmut7Y85F\nsHAC3NG9ZjI4g7ed/C8uOZTXWMUtfvDpeSk+BwQAjbsr8St0ASXK5/mN4/k4fKJ4\nd2wX2M1qHywvlW4pcyIJjVJXvylMHrw89gux2ZANlYmHBbhJO1lrS7A6oCjps6z3\naFx61e+TPg4F+aT1xZzj8gBdI3c9GviWPg4hEwAC3k/bKrq+56peZJcIGsqtOXPI\ntPYLyz2WVGdHfdxRuHpUF7Dpsncy+07YW1jr5z60qaHrX5MKsEE1aWKVqT7cOaWB\nabVfUJ9YCTH/jOodlymRyCvKdGkOiLZaH2zb0pmRKPBR2UHKp3h+ICeg3Tda1wUY\n6BBI0UXl2d7f/3QC2Tx6hBPRQVlLu1X84g9/vYb0EZ4JY1Y8AytkowVwUy4NxbLO\ndsZx7wT/dMLb5ytCg1zz7p/Tr+m/D/F3awb1bdc/i8f15+MkRCNGdL0iS5ZZR3ga\nYhqsJhcR/bSDc4jt7wHU0+8CEVqaK6cjVpn2AAH4/w10/AeGeboDuiUMYMDaC2Tv\nB8mp4Ej2v/5dQH6ggo3JjLDSQHiSb/YCpb5yJXACpDJS9XkL2nbN6144Rua7CGV2\nZkspCQZuexslDrB5WRKORDN3fE0DSyzjd+pJ+tafCtsMH1itaA4nx7kRWJ8y3skp\nS4gUeUuaGzVVpM+Aus2h\n=oVmI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T08:30:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/82fdc2d6333713d2fa1174891d897eeaf40ebdc2","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKDgyZmRjMmQ2MzMzNzEzZDJmYTExNzQ4OTFkODk3ZWVhZjQwZWJkYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6","sha":"12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6"}],"sha":"82fdc2d6333713d2fa1174891d897eeaf40ebdc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/82fdc2d6333713d2fa1174891d897eeaf40ebdc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:18:41Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:18:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(recording): force realtime transcription mode for Speechmatics sessions (#119)\n\nField measurement (gitops#3419): the user''s Speechmatics sessions ran\nwith transcriptionMode=''balanced'' leaking in from planner/bound-meeting\nstate, so the gateway live WebSocket was never opened and every word the\nuser saw came from the 5s REST aggregation windows\n(DirectSttForwardingDispatcher durationMs=5000 window_full,\nmodel=speechmatics-realtime-v2) — a fixed ~5s first-appearance lag.\nPreflight probes proved the live bridge itself connects and drains fine\n(terminal drained frames=0), so the only missing link was the mode gate.\n\n''balanced'' is only meaningful as the internal provider''s GPU-cost\nchoice; for the SaaS realtime provider the correct mode is always\nrealtime. The main process now normalizes provider=speechmatics to\ntranscriptionMode=realtime regardless of what the renderer sends, and\nlogs when it overrides a stale request.\n\nContract test updated: speechmatics + ''balanced'' now expects the live\nstream constructed and ''realtime'' forwarded to the gateway REST session.\nSuite 609/609, typecheck + lint + format clean.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e05cd6ec54c9e6f31dad53f0b7600d440e4c4d5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/e05cd6ec54c9e6f31dad53f0b7600d440e4c4d5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6","verification":{"payload":"tree e05cd6ec54c9e6f31dad53f0b7600d440e4c4d5a\nparent 8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785745121 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785745121 +0300\n\nfix(recording): force realtime transcription mode for Speechmatics sessions (#119)\n\nField measurement (gitops#3419): the user''s Speechmatics sessions ran\nwith transcriptionMode=''balanced'' leaking in from planner/bound-meeting\nstate, so the gateway live WebSocket was never opened and every word the\nuser saw came from the 5s REST aggregation windows\n(DirectSttForwardingDispatcher durationMs=5000 window_full,\nmodel=speechmatics-realtime-v2) — a fixed ~5s first-appearance lag.\nPreflight probes proved the live bridge itself connects and drains fine\n(terminal drained frames=0), so the only missing link was the mode gate.\n\n''balanced'' is only meaningful as the internal provider''s GPU-cost\nchoice; for the SaaS realtime provider the correct mode is always\nrealtime. The main process now normalizes provider=speechmatics to\ntranscriptionMode=realtime regardless of what the renderer sends, and\nlogs when it overrides a stale request.\n\nContract test updated: speechmatics + ''balanced'' now expects the live\nstream constructed and ''realtime'' forwarded to the gateway REST session.\nSuite 609/609, typecheck + lint + format clean.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcE7hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAySgQAGZLAxw0JamGXxR8w7bC4UVt\nIOInsS8Sox+cjjzDYrChxaBQRV/kzhJCezHQTrIPouD5FyknGRv4zCO7QPF6Ot1A\nUTuvKxsIj3d6YAQaIgy3ACnapGxe2ijCUHKLDHMm6q6DXvZ9xrbXGFuWX5b4wfEJ\nS8zAwh0UOC2j167soWUJ++I5Lr7mTdtXeq4Eyp7e7ZW9IQCGDUv2s7G5zep5A9UL\nwoyVzYROQXweGJORPwCGUWaxtVW/9gxCKde3ANHaqe05piLGF169cS/U+FNSL4wo\n7KN4LRBsQwqks15mTwiXT7LPHubtB0rYuJ2IYnCO9fmVnXuKjwW5K6eYQKKkBpbT\nysp4YUOChqphRi3ZEKONnbLFh02RRCenvRoOGfWRFuLGkk+yibnoHfI3ei91XzAJ\n8av6cIlxeDrcIvDt6aazs1jhFLIVLKj5f6y1hKvPVbIoN40GYon5dYFrZU3Nlaw5\n6zxA+LPuz4DH/59clgK6NIw9n+UhnpzWoUAvdFRdna3uLmWIbpDbhvjM41BmqgRo\npEqT7ivLuJsaNehxekaLVXpz1XQCeZpfYTnmGTC0VZ/TkP2gI0mNfGVlqLV/FsVF\nMk/WlMXRRrtvzVCZSQZ59yUbU5q4N8ErE3nvv0CtKwRe7LbGUwU8PVrkzS3WBGVb\nFR83J1U2CoPUAJv5j9tW\n=VgHP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T08:18:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKDEyZWE3M2ZiNjA5OThjNzBjNGY0YjJkNWIwOTI1N2FlNmFlNGI0ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d","sha":"8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d"}],"sha":"12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/12ea73fb60998c70c4f4b2d5b09257ae6ae4b4f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T07:54:17Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T07:54:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(transcript): anchor the live partial as a single trailing tail row (#118)\n\nUser field report (2026-08-03, live dev run): word-by-word tracking worked\nuntil the FIRST final landed, then the display went sentence-at-a-time.\n\nRoot cause: a partial''s startedAtMs was computed as receivedAt-elapsed,\nwhich pins every partial to roughly the SESSION START. Once a final with\na source-ranged (later) startedAtMs exists, the partial sorts BEFORE it,\nstops being the trailing segment, and the fluent view''s tail goes dark —\nonly finals remain visible. Partials also shared the window id space with\nfinals, risking silent drops behind the FINAL>DRAFT rank guard.\n\nFix (industry two-lane contract, survey §1.3):\n- electron main: partials now emit a single mutable row per transport\n  epoch (id live-<session>-<epoch>-tail, windowSeq null) stamped with\n  receivedAtMs — always trailing, replaced in place on every partial;\n  finals keep their immutable window-keyed identity.\n- turn-flow: when a final lands, the stale tail briefly repeats words the\n  final now covers (until the next partial refreshes it) — hide the tail\n  while the last committed paragraph already contains its word window.\n\nTests: 2 new turn-flow cases; suite 609/609, typecheck+lint+format clean.\nLive-verified in the running dev app after main-process restart.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff6dc4812862fbe4f8fbcec0fc967cb39dfd19a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/ff6dc4812862fbe4f8fbcec0fc967cb39dfd19a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d","verification":{"payload":"tree ff6dc4812862fbe4f8fbcec0fc967cb39dfd19a2\nparent a4530dda8af6254e375b871ae5dc11e18867f134\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785743657 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785743657 +0300\n\nfix(transcript): anchor the live partial as a single trailing tail row (#118)\n\nUser field report (2026-08-03, live dev run): word-by-word tracking worked\nuntil the FIRST final landed, then the display went sentence-at-a-time.\n\nRoot cause: a partial''s startedAtMs was computed as receivedAt-elapsed,\nwhich pins every partial to roughly the SESSION START. Once a final with\na source-ranged (later) startedAtMs exists, the partial sorts BEFORE it,\nstops being the trailing segment, and the fluent view''s tail goes dark —\nonly finals remain visible. Partials also shared the window id space with\nfinals, risking silent drops behind the FINAL>DRAFT rank guard.\n\nFix (industry two-lane contract, survey §1.3):\n- electron main: partials now emit a single mutable row per transport\n  epoch (id live-<session>-<epoch>-tail, windowSeq null) stamped with\n  receivedAtMs — always trailing, replaced in place on every partial;\n  finals keep their immutable window-keyed identity.\n- turn-flow: when a final lands, the stale tail briefly repeats words the\n  final now covers (until the next partial refreshes it) — hide the tail\n  while the last committed paragraph already contains its word window.\n\nTests: 2 new turn-flow cases; suite 609/609, typecheck+lint+format clean.\nLive-verified in the running dev app after main-process restart.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcEkpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4WsQAKyk1u/JMqjNmLhSD1A1Qttv\nylDtfwcDD11pwMTx9A75n+Y+6pg/56XLmMX3N1SOrChOo4Bjcn1aUfGX/bVA+dDm\naktmVrf2MtNmwQPMj615fcWed1Fr6LX1Mifw9O/DR420te1mUK0DmUarIVrQGNpY\nKXP70MhWImVz5+HdGKmsclECeudzx42djgcvOk8SK7ANc8p5i3f6mWL/u2VhnMlY\nJUfomDR0LYrDywnCqSm+fY4fyMSlG6rt23HsDWEhoy0c9GqOi/CrwYMVL19/TWI0\n6Ulq6tL6IwUvtycwW/nat1rqdyTdsLyn25bYQvZIPKFkUmkeLEKJyJv3DOe4XnU7\nBmIJXxpWwRuxStImJIuy31iUqUBQ8TM7lwj5VB8AflePaxdNW6lwoYvkvozNm51P\nKh9VgVjdV1t/DHt4AG2HGijJ/Z/tcx35t61s5ZmJGDdpyF81ARJbM71dzvo8X4GN\nW34bXZxqYwajp5s2tOGmGttgUdjqrE57+uRtz0kDr9derKHqDyGig1aOdL3SfRpB\nnHH/AFT9ccGWLd53QpRaaa6cmP96J59KyHQjVVnWoBxlxjtPqnLjB6ijNaZe7fmi\nJCfbK2JnGz/nMmQgNYCjZdx87TiI71th0O7REi5ezO2h7CmGowhY0N2JiB60nFgC\n35OkKGcUJHoX1iYCbdzn\n=2EWS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T07:54:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKDgyNTFhNDRjMzUyZTg2MDRiZWI1M2FmNjczZDYyYjEwZDZhZWU3MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/a4530dda8af6254e375b871ae5dc11e18867f134","sha":"a4530dda8af6254e375b871ae5dc11e18867f134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/a4530dda8af6254e375b871ae5dc11e18867f134"}],"sha":"8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/8251a44c352e8604beb53af673d62b10d6aee70d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/a4530dda8af6254e375b871ae5dc11e18867f134/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T06:59:41Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T06:59:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(transcript): Akıcı canlı görünüm — cümle-sınırlı akış + satır-içi kelime-kelime kuyruk (#117)\n\n* feat(transcript): fluent live view — sentence-bounded flow with inline word-by-word tail\n\nUsers watched the live transcript arrive as a new metadata-laden card\nevery 2-5s commit, with sentences fragmented across cards (gitops#3419).\nIndustry reference UIs (Speechmatics portal, Deepgram/Azure guidance —\nsee gitops docs/faz24-realtime-stt-industry-survey.md) render two lanes\ninstead: committed text flows into one paragraph until a sentence\nterminator is certain, and the mutable partial tail updates in place at\nthe end of the flow.\n\nThis adds that as the DEFAULT view while keeping the existing per-segment\nreview cards intact behind a new ''Akıcı | Satırlar'' toggle (row view still\nowns the edit/review actions):\n\n- src/transcript/turn-flow.ts: pure fold of a turn''s segments into flow\n  paragraphs; a paragraph closes ONLY on sentence-final punctuation\n  (never on elapsed time — turn boundaries upstream already handle\n  speaker change / long gaps); trailing draft/stabilizing segments become\n  the live tail, mid-turn drafts (REST fallback windows) stay in the flow\n  marked pending so no content is lost.\n- TranscriptPanel: view toggle + fluent turn body (single speaker header,\n  flowing paragraphs, dimmed italic tail with the existing live caret).\n- Tests: 8 new turn-flow unit tests + fluent default render test; row-view\n  tests now switch views explicitly. 607/607 passing; lint + typecheck clean.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style: prettier format pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c39a0c0afa28278f232bb8dc54e8182177160cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/9c39a0c0afa28278f232bb8dc54e8182177160cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/a4530dda8af6254e375b871ae5dc11e18867f134","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c39a0c0afa28278f232bb8dc54e8182177160cd\nparent 2745f565e84472d020aef77678ed701845ea2351\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785740381 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785740381 +0300\n\nfeat(transcript): Akıcı canlı görünüm — cümle-sınırlı akış + satır-içi kelime-kelime kuyruk (#117)\n\n* feat(transcript): fluent live view — sentence-bounded flow with inline word-by-word tail\n\nUsers watched the live transcript arrive as a new metadata-laden card\nevery 2-5s commit, with sentences fragmented across cards (gitops#3419).\nIndustry reference UIs (Speechmatics portal, Deepgram/Azure guidance —\nsee gitops docs/faz24-realtime-stt-industry-survey.md) render two lanes\ninstead: committed text flows into one paragraph until a sentence\nterminator is certain, and the mutable partial tail updates in place at\nthe end of the flow.\n\nThis adds that as the DEFAULT view while keeping the existing per-segment\nreview cards intact behind a new ''Akıcı | Satırlar'' toggle (row view still\nowns the edit/review actions):\n\n- src/transcript/turn-flow.ts: pure fold of a turn''s segments into flow\n  paragraphs; a paragraph closes ONLY on sentence-final punctuation\n  (never on elapsed time — turn boundaries upstream already handle\n  speaker change / long gaps); trailing draft/stabilizing segments become\n  the live tail, mid-turn drafts (REST fallback windows) stay in the flow\n  marked pending so no content is lost.\n- TranscriptPanel: view toggle + fluent turn body (single speaker header,\n  flowing paragraphs, dimmed italic tail with the existing live caret).\n- Tests: 8 new turn-flow unit tests + fluent default render test; row-view\n  tests now switch views explicitly. 607/607 passing; lint + typecheck clean.\n\nTracked by platform-k8s-gitops#3419\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style: prettier format pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcDxdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZf0QAIh1PFQtoWQCDYDuSd01n5Iq\nlDaL9ANhdAC682Sb4SNU97kyFjMlJCyoyEJCvEnZkDB6FL4tY0BasJr+HhtFJV8A\nMnwOex9Sw84YeAfI/Y5Fphebq4VN56vmHrcUp/aVn2/4mUAzW4NLpUG0r1pOobA2\nuyJI8CmDnCoOYRHKcaa7wN1FsOG68XS2JPZwFpU0k082FsFDptsS3O/bkpAkGNPG\nk+kn9C3BJhADtouZZ2H8lq8zuf/golBdctLeggSWHRcxLd0lSEcReNK86w5+rHDV\nLnkZ1y+XEQCY7VNeLCbqQXniwTQCh0DIGjsISnDMyztoHav3km7eKub9DJMX2MjV\nIy680Ju9NnA1ezjbjQclUKR9RLU2BJ1iiA5X1KwaJDBfu1d/0fIzr7SSvTk7Lo/+\nYRzrlYe9QeWfhh49endHQdI4wmSP9OhqlF4EYKR0M46yz0+/opvDPwCYpa2kE1V1\nxD2Y7wcB1q7hrcmYGIdUm3aggspVhIT0CZymljic/jCGoqDQQKIOzZuWLGs8LNvB\nPlYLALHc7xF1Bym91emMLlxro+nEISgGw7f1yD3+uUQZC/GvAXxgBiQ6NWhLZOpI\nDkJCCVO4FPP7afrnXtWFWkBhovXdWBFzQ4Fgknr05fRfcElTeG5p7ZPvMmFonZRC\nULmlgWLo6gL+XXOnigB6\n=yPRY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T06:59:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/u