platform-desktop/commits/b98a75b201036ec6e1bb70c56adf7b15711ff1b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/08a69fd0d1bf38f3ab51041ef802ef64cebdf2f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:42:33Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:42:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(desktop): live-analysis SSE consumer + LiveAnalysisPanel (Faz 24 İ3) (#79)\n\nWires the Faz 24 canlı analiz iterasyon 3 slice: platform-desktop now\nsubscribes to meeting-ai''s `GET /analyze/live/stream/{meetingId}` (see\nplatform-ai #270), unfolds each SSE `event: analysis` frame in the main\nprocess, and renders the latest partial/final result in a new panel.\nCombined with #270 the desktop viewer sees canlı özet/karar/aksiyon land\nwithout any meeting-service persistence round-trip.\n\nMain process (electron/services/meeting/live-analysis-stream.ts):\n\n- `LiveAnalysisSubscriber` — reconnecting SSE reader using native fetch\n  streaming (Node 22+ undici; no `eventsource` npm dep).\n- Manual SSE frame parser (`parseSseChunk`) — spec-correct handling of\n  LF/CRLF, comment lines, multi-line `data:`, single-leading-space strip,\n  and chunk-boundary carry.\n- Exponential reconnect backoff (default 500ms → 30s cap) with abort-\n  aware sleep so `stop()` unwinds the loop cleanly.\n- Listener callbacks NEVER break the loop: `onFrame` / `onStatus`\n  throws are swallowed. Non-2xx and non-JSON `data:` payloads become\n  `error` status frames, not exceptions.\n\nIPC (electron/ipc/meeting.ts + electron/preload.ts):\n\n- `meeting:live-analysis-start` / `-stop` — idempotent per meetingId,\n  keyed by an in-process `Map<string, LiveAnalysisSubscriber>`.\n- `meeting:live-analysis-frame` + `-status` — broadcast to every window''s\n  webContents so multiple renderer views can observe the same stream.\n- `stopAllLiveAnalysisSubscribers()` invoked on `app.before-quit` so the\n  fetch loop and reconnect timers don''t keep the app alive past user quit.\n\nRenderer (src/intelligence/use-live-analysis.ts + src/components/…):\n\n- `useLiveAnalysis(meetingId, api?)` hook — subscribe on mount / meeting\n  change, tear down on unmount / null meetingId. Keeps the HIGHEST\n  version (matches the meeting-ai contract: a late lower-version partial\n  never regresses the panel). Resets version tracking on meetingId\n  change so a switch from meeting A (v10) to meeting B (v1) does not\n  drop B''s first frame.\n- `LiveAnalysisPanel` — read-only viewer with:\n    * status pill (idle / connecting / open / closed / error) so a broken\n      relay is diagnosable in-app;\n    * `Kısmi (vN)` badge on `is_partial=true` frames (final removes it);\n    * summary + decisions + action_items rendered from the raw payload\n      (schema drift stays visible instead of being silently coerced);\n    * KVKK redaction count footer when the analyzer redacted spans;\n    * `aria-live=\"polite\"` so screen readers announce updates without\n      hijacking focus.\n- Preserved existing `SummaryPanel` — the canonical final view is\n  unchanged; this new panel is the LIVE companion.\n\nTests:\n\n- Main: 13 tests — parser (7) + subscriber loop (6). Uses a mocked\n  `fetch` returning a controllable `ReadableStream` so the reader loop\n  is exercised without a real hop.\n- Renderer hook: 6 tests — mount/unmount, status transitions, highest-\n  version wins, cross-meeting isolation, tear-down on null, no\n  cross-meeting version leak on rerender.\n- Panel: 5 tests — empty state, waiting state, live partial rendering\n  with badge, badge hidden on final, error copy on connection failure.\n- Existing App.test / capture.test electronAPI mocks extended with the 4\n  new meeting methods so the full 497-test suite stays green.\n\nContract check summary:\n  npx tsc --noEmit                     ✓\n  npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.electron.json   ✓\n  npm run lint                         ✓\n  npm run format:check                 ✓\n  npx vitest run                       ✓ 497/497 (was 483; +14 net)\n\nFollow-ups (not in this PR):\n  - İ4: audio-gateway TranscriptAggregator + cadenced /analyze/live POST\n  - İ5: end-to-end acceptance smoke (browser MCP + curl SSE parse)\n\nRef: platform-ai#270 (SSE relay endpoint), Faz 24 Zeynep 2026-07-20\nkapsam kararı.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c611ba763cfb2ed5d206a8ae212515773bbccfea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/c611ba763cfb2ed5d206a8ae212515773bbccfea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/08a69fd0d1bf38f3ab51041ef802ef64cebdf2f6","verification":{"payload":"tree c611ba763cfb2ed5d206a8ae212515773bbccfea\nparent 7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1784590953 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784590953 +0300\n\nfeat(desktop): live-analysis SSE consumer + LiveAnalysisPanel (Faz 24 İ3) (#79)\n\nWires the Faz 24 canlı analiz iterasyon 3 slice: platform-desktop now\nsubscribes to meeting-ai''s `GET /analyze/live/stream/{meetingId}` (see\nplatform-ai #270), unfolds each SSE `event: analysis` frame in the main\nprocess, and renders the latest partial/final result in a new panel.\nCombined with #270 the desktop viewer sees canlı özet/karar/aksiyon land\nwithout any meeting-service persistence round-trip.\n\nMain process (electron/services/meeting/live-analysis-stream.ts):\n\n- `LiveAnalysisSubscriber` — reconnecting SSE reader using native fetch\n  streaming (Node 22+ undici; no `eventsource` npm dep).\n- Manual SSE frame parser (`parseSseChunk`) — spec-correct handling of\n  LF/CRLF, comment lines, multi-line `data:`, single-leading-space strip,\n  and chunk-boundary carry.\n- Exponential reconnect backoff (default 500ms → 30s cap) with abort-\n  aware sleep so `stop()` unwinds the loop cleanly.\n- Listener callbacks NEVER break the loop: `onFrame` / `onStatus`\n  throws are swallowed. Non-2xx and non-JSON `data:` payloads become\n  `error` status frames, not exceptions.\n\nIPC (electron/ipc/meeting.ts + electron/preload.ts):\n\n- `meeting:live-analysis-start` / `-stop` — idempotent per meetingId,\n  keyed by an in-process `Map<string, LiveAnalysisSubscriber>`.\n- `meeting:live-analysis-frame` + `-status` — broadcast to every window''s\n  webContents so multiple renderer views can observe the same stream.\n- `stopAllLiveAnalysisSubscribers()` invoked on `app.before-quit` so the\n  fetch loop and reconnect timers don''t keep the app alive past user quit.\n\nRenderer (src/intelligence/use-live-analysis.ts + src/components/…):\n\n- `useLiveAnalysis(meetingId, api?)` hook — subscribe on mount / meeting\n  change, tear down on unmount / null meetingId. Keeps the HIGHEST\n  version (matches the meeting-ai contract: a late lower-version partial\n  never regresses the panel). Resets version tracking on meetingId\n  change so a switch from meeting A (v10) to meeting B (v1) does not\n  drop B''s first frame.\n- `LiveAnalysisPanel` — read-only viewer with:\n    * status pill (idle / connecting / open / closed / error) so a broken\n      relay is diagnosable in-app;\n    * `Kısmi (vN)` badge on `is_partial=true` frames (final removes it);\n    * summary + decisions + action_items rendered from the raw payload\n      (schema drift stays visible instead of being silently coerced);\n    * KVKK redaction count footer when the analyzer redacted spans;\n    * `aria-live=\"polite\"` so screen readers announce updates without\n      hijacking focus.\n- Preserved existing `SummaryPanel` — the canonical final view is\n  unchanged; this new panel is the LIVE companion.\n\nTests:\n\n- Main: 13 tests — parser (7) + subscriber loop (6). Uses a mocked\n  `fetch` returning a controllable `ReadableStream` so the reader loop\n  is exercised without a real hop.\n- Renderer hook: 6 tests — mount/unmount, status transitions, highest-\n  version wins, cross-meeting isolation, tear-down on null, no\n  cross-meeting version leak on rerender.\n- Panel: 5 tests — empty state, waiting state, live partial rendering\n  with badge, badge hidden on final, error copy on connection failure.\n- Existing App.test / capture.test electronAPI mocks extended with the 4\n  new meeting methods so the full 497-test suite stays green.\n\nContract check summary:\n  npx tsc --noEmit                     ✓\n  npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.electron.json   ✓\n  npm run lint                         ✓\n  npm run format:check                 ✓\n  npx vitest run                       ✓ 497/497 (was 483; +14 net)\n\nFollow-ups (not in this PR):\n  - İ4: audio-gateway TranscriptAggregator + cadenced /analyze/live POST\n  - İ5: end-to-end acceptance smoke (browser MCP + curl SSE parse)\n\nRef: platform-ai#270 (SSE relay endpoint), Faz 24 Zeynep 2026-07-20\nkapsam kararı.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQB