.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0","sha":"7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0"}],"sha":"08a69fd0d1bf38f3ab51041ef802ef64cebdf2f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/08a69fd0d1bf38f3ab51041ef802ef64cebdf2f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:03:03Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:03:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(security): audit hygiene — dependabot + prod-focused threshold (kalıcı fix) (#65)\n\n* chore(security): audit hygiene — dependabot + prod-focused threshold\n\nSymptom: PR #63 + #64 each stalled on `npm audit --audit-level=moderate`\nagainst rolling transitive advisories (brace-expansion, js-yaml, tar) that\nhad no code path in this app but blocked the pipeline. Each `npm audit fix`\ncommit was a short-lived symptom fix — the next new advisory reproduced\nthe same friction inside days.\n\nLong-term fix (2 layers):\n\n1. Threshold + scope aligned to blast radius:\n   - `security:audit` → `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high`\n     Blocks CI on high+ advisories that reach the packaged runtime (the\n     electron production tree). Dev-only tooling advisories become\n     `security:audit:full` — reported, never blocking.\n   - `security:audit:full` (new) preserves the `--audit-level=moderate`\n     full-tree scan for local review; a follow-up can wire it to a\n     scheduled `security-audit` job that comments on the tracking issue\n     rather than failing PR CI.\n\n2. Dependabot v2 (`.github/dependabot.yml`) — 3 update channels:\n   - npm weekly (Monday 07:00 Europe/Istanbul) grouped patch+minor, majors\n     individual — one review decision per week for routine deps.\n   - npm daily security channel — new advisories raise a PR the same day,\n     bypasses the weekly cadence.\n   - github-actions monthly — pin-by-sha updates for the workflow YAMLs.\n   Grouping keeps review load one-PR/week; the security channel keeps\n   critical fixes from waiting.\n\nPost-change: `npm run security:audit` = 0 vulnerabilities;\n`npm run security:audit:full` = 0 vulnerabilities (baseline clean; the\nchange is in what future advisories will and won''t block).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(format): prettier normalise dependabot.yml\n\nSame-PR fix: added dependabot.yml didn''t pass `prettier --check`.\nRan `prettier --write`; no semantic change (whitespace only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dependabot): remove duplicate npm entry — v2 uniqueness rule\n\nDependabot rejected the config: \"Update configs must have a unique\ncombination of ''package-ecosystem'', ''directory'', and ''target-branch''.\nEcosystem ''npm'' has overlapping directories.\"\n\nThe previous two-entry design (weekly + daily security channel) violated\nv2''s uniqueness rule. It was also redundant — dependabot opens security\nPRs the moment an advisory is published regardless of the weekly cadence\n(dependabot-security-updates default behaviour); a separate channel adds\nno acceleration.\n\nKept as one weekly npm entry + github-actions monthly. Added a docstring\ncomment explaining the security-fix default so a future maintainer does\nnot re-add the duplicate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2cb683b261e3686d802676feac762e8ef70b7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/d2cb683b261e3686d802676feac762e8ef70b7a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0","verification":{"payload":"tree d2cb683b261e3686d802676feac762e8ef70b7a5\nparent f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1784588583 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784588583 +0300\n\nchore(security): audit hygiene — dependabot + prod-focused threshold (kalıcı fix) (#65)\n\n* chore(security): audit hygiene — dependabot + prod-focused threshold\n\nSymptom: PR #63 + #64 each stalled on `npm audit --audit-level=moderate`\nagainst rolling transitive advisories (brace-expansion, js-yaml, tar) that\nhad no code path in this app but blocked the pipeline. Each `npm audit fix`\ncommit was a short-lived symptom fix — the next new advisory reproduced\nthe same friction inside days.\n\nLong-term fix (2 layers):\n\n1. Threshold + scope aligned to blast radius:\n   - `security:audit` → `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high`\n     Blocks CI on high+ advisories that reach the packaged runtime (the\n     electron production tree). Dev-only tooling advisories become\n     `security:audit:full` — reported, never blocking.\n   - `security:audit:full` (new) preserves the `--audit-level=moderate`\n     full-tree scan for local review; a follow-up can wire it to a\n     scheduled `security-audit` job that comments on the tracking issue\n     rather than failing PR CI.\n\n2. Dependabot v2 (`.github/dependabot.yml`) — 3 update channels:\n   - npm weekly (Monday 07:00 Europe/Istanbul) grouped patch+minor, majors\n     individual — one review decision per week for routine deps.\n   - npm daily security channel — new advisories raise a PR the same day,\n     bypasses the weekly cadence.\n   - github-actions monthly — pin-by-sha updates for the workflow YAMLs.\n   Grouping keeps review load one-PR/week; the security channel keeps\n   critical fixes from waiting.\n\nPost-change: `npm run security:audit` = 0 vulnerabilities;\n`npm run security:audit:full` = 0 vulnerabilities (baseline clean; the\nchange is in what future advisories will and won''t block).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(format): prettier normalise dependabot.yml\n\nSame-PR fix: added dependabot.yml didn''t pass `prettier --check`.\nRan `prettier --write`; no semantic change (whitespace only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dependabot): remove duplicate npm entry — v2 uniqueness rule\n\nDependabot rejected the config: \"Update configs must have a unique\ncombination of ''package-ecosystem'', ''directory'', and ''target-branch''.\nEcosystem ''npm'' has overlapping directories.\"\n\nThe previous two-entry design (weekly + daily security channel) violated\nv2''s uniqueness rule. It was also redundant — dependabot opens security\nPRs the moment an advisory is published regardless of the weekly cadence\n(dependabot-security-updates default behaviour); a separate channel adds\nno acceleration.\n\nKept as one weekly npm entry + github-actions monthly. Added a docstring\ncomment explaining the security-fix default so a future maintainer does\nnot re-add the duplicate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXqknCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhK0QADwHz2o+XocgMBpPtUOeBKC3\ncE957u7E8N59fV1oFuiI3plrW57+f8aQLtlhx51Hss0iVBM+/vZhG5DaRtA1gbxO\nUrW02fJgJ4FbfqMTy3hooGLSKWC8s/yAI2fDIEW6hYNoJF5D5GzfPinOW7wytRul\niJrBztFCHSWFrMlqYieQvi0uV+/b7lE1qUCz/18RDm2AmzOfAZEiMls7gCE2gKFT\nE3TlOOzOJH1ZZMzYIjSF1XzFn8xXZh+5ZCLALFfH2fVv12jxwWxQlHlUU5j036n+\nMn/4T5zvZstelfmC6dYjND06AYEuKXBXFOA7MhmAYFCJuzBPnOTxJhjQ9wt4YJOb\n8lSskEqbEtMgs04FZuOSdXnuEq03nOQDMjVd3d4/GxdP+q3fDM7VG8t1UY6yiM5q\np9BClwH+tflnAhYil7UNlOX+6G2O4gco0/WXkS4oLewN2qw9rLESB04A6zJ310mW\nmWOzk9y6jjG7TaiG9Lvfh3h1q4+w1b1RDtwc6UTdzpE7nVJ6WzeQuAabl1Hl/yMG\nh8qF/J9h9wTJJ85e34uO5+sIRI77Ny5eezEGn5wTyAZEFDWfnoWBJ551S0JHJrkj\n9II4OEGlKrzMz8WUOurz3yZNwvXkJwq51DUj8mQBHd+6s6LpY8K4nnIYQCUxpksl\nmI23MTrmqFpvCziD9Xsx\n=pZiv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-20T23:03:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKDdhMTQ0YjU3NDk1YTJhYjdhNWMwZGZhZDhlNjVkNzhhNTE4NDBiZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c","sha":"f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c"}],"sha":"7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/7a144b57495a2ab7a5c0dfad8e65d78a51840bd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:58:31Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:58:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(build): standardise Windows artifactName to Linux/Mac dashed contract (#66)\n\nSymptom that surfaced this: PR #64 shipped a workflow verify that had to\ntolerate productName-with-space defaults for Windows because the Windows\ntarget lacked `artifactName`. Mac and Linux both already set\n`Meeting-Intelligence-${version}-${arch}.${ext}` — Windows was the drift.\n\nLong-term fix: bring Windows onto the same contract, then pin the CI\nverify glob to the dashed pattern (drift guard).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. `package.json` — electron-builder Windows config:\n   - `win.artifactName = \"Meeting-Intelligence-${version}-${arch}.${ext}\"`\n     — matches Linux/Mac line-for-line.\n   - `nsis.artifactName = \"Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-${version}-${arch}.${ext}\"`\n     — installer keeps its `Setup` marker (users + updater expect it).\n   - `portable.artifactName` — explicit even though it collapses to the\n     top-level `win.artifactName`, so removing the top-level does not\n     silently rename the portable.\n\n2. `.github/workflows/package-windows.yml` — verify globs now pin the\n   dashed contract (`Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-*.exe` for the installer,\n   `Meeting-Intelligence-*.exe` minus Setup for the portable). If the\n   contract regresses (someone removes `win.artifactName`), CI fails with\n   a clear error rather than silently accepting the old space-based\n   filenames.\n\nRationale — this is a drift guard, not a naming preference. Two naming\nconventions in the same repo invite the exact class of bug that made\nPR #64 necessary (glob mismatch between platforms). One naming, pinned in\nCI, no glob tolerance.\n\nExpected filenames after this lands (electron-builder --win --x64):\n- `Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-0.1.4-x64.exe`\n- `Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-0.1.4-x64.exe.blockmap`\n- `Meeting-Intelligence-0.1.4-x64.exe`\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6476877286d15adb49a3fee901061139ae79f180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/6476877286d15adb49a3fee901061139ae79f180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c","verification":{"payload":"tree 6476877286d15adb49a3fee901061139ae79f180\nparent fd39ea12641b3cf7c1ae0beea09ffdd8a0af2fe5\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1784588311 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784588311 +0300\n\nchore(build): standardise Windows artifactName to Linux/Mac dashed contract (#66)\n\nSymptom that surfaced this: PR #64 shipped a workflow verify that had to\ntolerate productName-with-space defaults for Windows because the Windows\ntarget lacked `artifactName`. Mac and Linux both already set\n`Meeting-Intelligence-${version}-${arch}.${ext}` — Windows was the drift.\n\nLong-term fix: bring Windows onto the same contract, then pin the CI\nverify glob to the dashed pattern (drift guard).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. `package.json` — electron-builder Windows config:\n   - `win.artifactName = \"Meeting-Intelligence-${version}-${arch}.${ext}\"`\n     — matches Linux/Mac line-for-line.\n   - `nsis.artifactName = \"Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-${version}-${arch}.${ext}\"`\n     — installer keeps its `Setup` marker (users + updater expect it).\n   - `portable.artifactName` — explicit even though it collapses to the\n     top-level `win.artifactName`, so removing the top-level does not\n     silently rename the portable.\n\n2. `.github/workflows/package-windows.yml` — verify globs now pin the\n   dashed contract (`Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-*.exe` for the installer,\n   `Meeting-Intelligence-*.exe` minus Setup for the portable). If the\n   contract regresses (someone removes `win.artifactName`), CI fails with\n   a clear error rather than silently accepting the old space-based\n   filenames.\n\nRationale — this is a drift guard, not a naming preference. Two naming\nconventions in the same repo invite the exact class of bug that made\nPR #64 necessary (glob mismatch between platforms). One naming, pinned in\nCI, no glob tolerance.\n\nExpected filenames after this lands (electron-builder --win --x64):\n- `Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-0.1.4-x64.exe`\n- `Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-0.1.4-x64.exe.blockmap`\n- `Meeting-Intelligence-0.1.4-x64.exe`\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXqgXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADJUQAC4D+jBUiV1WCKCFPUoMXnla\n+63ZCNVbP+eh0jhDklzM/u7YFkLr+Es9ItGv8ni5/yZ2OQeAtEUeCdI87hBIe9D3\njZ1uCv4b3rmuTZzncNmSawhSb8DDzHXZarGr86PcgW22iVqY69CeVlWU5BKvKESM\noGFtlt2CiT6DQkFJYIbYncReMDCeGdok3YS7+S8bt9e9P80pQhMiTwvX6MBH77MV\n+DEtk+2xqwfSiE51bLtLEE8Up556DLqGTm+hiGZAjLuafai81QHPj6Ch1Of1X+pi\nVmqTm86o5h6BSSwz1VI93YIpNEaUAtFdh6ejHoKAD9KLLcqYdGGCUpm1Kqz4yzPY\nniiSdvLqACmAaO/FBzjhyFWjVgDgPiaZaKAroWdYJqyZIzipUpVWg9sBUXdzbbFv\n51FSfOMzlP1lVR0n8aI/yfy01n1YpnwHCWQ4pFdqm7tPAKwtVOL1Sr1iOsinhDc+\nSv2iQsh/zPUUISBlFFMCIF4sSgSbN595zM3dhsU3hwgfc+0Q05z5/D+VFuu11PIm\nVs4A9QFlnmgkn2656ev6DLP1poVckDrlo+uWL6c1Bzw9CoTl/WWiiamBQ0U+4K8j\nn7eAtu5iCTE3TFkFYi+BYFwTNXsPYmjwGA9bG+MCmCCdkAGsXj/KhgFgvtGUsmj5\nYEPKY4+IrVue9y2Muxzb\n=757H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-20T22:58:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKGYzZjhmYTYzYzlkMGMwNGY0MDIzNTEyNTMyOThiOGNkYjMyMmIwMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/fd39ea12641b3cf7c1ae0beea09ffdd8a0af2fe5","sha":"fd39ea12641b3cf7c1ae0beea09ffdd8a0af2fe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/fd39ea12641b3cf7c1ae0beea09ffdd8a0af2fe5"}],"sha":"f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/f3f8fa63c9d0c04f402351253298b8cdb322b02c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/fd39ea12641b3cf7c1ae0beea09ffdd8a0af2fe5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:24:12Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:24:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(build): windows package verify+upload glob for productName-based names (#64)\n\n* fix(build): windows package verify+upload glob for productName-based names\n\nThe Linux mirror workflow #63 shipped verify globs assuming a dashed\nartifactName (Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-<v>.exe), but no artifactName\nis set for Windows so electron-builder emits productName-based names\nwith spaces: \"Meeting Intelligence Setup 0.1.4.exe\" (NSIS) and\n\"Meeting Intelligence 0.1.4.exe\" (portable). The first Windows build\n(run 29783144360) succeeded through electron-builder but the verify\nstep exit-1''d on the missing dashed pattern.\n\nFix:\n- Verify: glob on *Setup*.exe for the installer and *.exe minus Setup\n  for the portable. Space-tolerant, works whether/when artifactName is\n  standardised later.\n- Upload artifact: include all *.exe + *.exe.blockmap + latest.yml\n  (electron-updater delta patches) alongside BUILD_METADATA.txt.\n\nA follow-up can standardise artifactName across Linux/Mac/Windows if\nwe want dashed names everywhere; keeping this fix narrow so the smoke\npackage for Zeynep (Bulgu 2 fix #61) lands today.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): npm audit fix — tar critical (rolling advisory)\n\nNew critical advisory published today (tar <=7.5.18, 4 GHSA IDs)\nblocked this PR''s build. Same fix pattern as #63: lock-file only,\n0 vulnerabilities after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"588ee2b1e90b323bca628af4e148eb0c9c8ee1f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/588ee2b1e90b323bca628af4e148eb0c9c8ee1f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/fd39ea12641b3cf7c1ae0beea09ffdd8a0af2fe5","verification":{"payload":"tree 588ee2b1e90b323bca628af4e148eb0c9c8ee1f7\nparent efd24b22d3f654cfa829b9ea1bdb65e58054cff0\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1784586252 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784586252 +0300\n\nfix(build): windows package verify+upload glob for productName-based names (#64)\n\n* fix(build): windows package verify+upload glob for productName-based names\n\nThe Linux mirror workflow #63 shipped verify globs assuming a dashed\nartifactName (Meeting-Intelligence-Setup-<v>.exe), but no artifactName\nis set for Windows so electron-builder emits productName-based names\nwith spaces: \"Meeting Intelligence Setup 0.1.4.exe\" (NSIS) and\n\"Meeting Intelligence 0.1.4.exe\" (portable). The first Windows build\n(run 29783144360) succeeded through electron-builder but the verify\nstep exit-1''d on the missing dashed pattern.\n\nFix:\n- Verify: glob on *Setup*.exe for the installer and *.exe minus Setup\n  for the portable. Space-tolerant, works whether/when artifactName is\n  standardised later.\n- Upload artifact: include all *.exe + *.exe.blockmap + latest.yml\n  (electron-updater delta patches) alongside BUILD_METADATA.txt.\n\nA follow-up can standardise artifactName across Linux/Mac/Windows if\nwe want dashed names everywhere; keeping this fix narrow so the smoke\npackage for Zeynep (Bulgu 2 fix #61) lands today.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): npm audit fix — tar critical (rolling advisory)\n\nNew critical advisory published today (tar <=7.5.18, 4 GHSA IDs)\nblocked this PR''s build. Same fix pattern as #63: lock-file only,\n0 vulnerabilities after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXqAMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPnoQAK0HCzUUwa/e1H9oghwlYvlB\nP2ZjOBEgkKpNpPwMQVHKueixRVz5159n20gTCO+fJ3rXn3Z2j6Hphhf7a0A/po03\nWgp2LoapXqrltS/FM2XYEa9si05FtGJ37RgtMeI/x95ZgPHiRpRzI5ZuGKhWWdBJ\nTv6Ul1lV2Fg6M+aK/gXcbNkXcnZH8GjT+bjIjWa3KLiEcaq14QE4I7XnWIBJ9nRo\nxO+h/oe+5Dc1aHky