noEmit clean (renderer + electron), vitest 29 files / 262 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d22c062c6ea1b3821dc706884e86cddf0cc55f7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/d22c062c6ea1b3821dc706884e86cddf0cc55f7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/fbddcc14bfac748eabf5e6bb6ed5a91a6b83591f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/fbddcc14bfac748eabf5e6bb6ed5a91a6b83591f","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTQJ9oAKGZiZGRjYzE0YmZhYzc0OGVhYmY1ZTZiYjZlZDVhOTFhNmI4MzU5MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/874ec01ddaf5c713888b9f465ec9a40f876a39d0","sha":"874ec01ddaf5c713888b9f465ec9a40f876a39d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/874ec01ddaf5c713888b9f465ec9a40f876a39d0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commit/3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f","sha":"3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f"}],"sha":"fbddcc14bfac748eabf5e6bb6ed5a91a6b83591f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/fbddcc14bfac748eabf5e6bb6ed5a91a6b83591f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244165292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zeynep-serban","id":244165292,"login":"zeynep-serban","node_id":"U_kgDODo2qrA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T08:37:44Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T08:37:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(desktop): packaging groundwork — mac entitlements, linux rpm, auto-update wiring (#7, #8, #10, #11) (#36)\n\n* feat(desktop): packaging groundwork — mac entitlements, linux rpm/desktop-entry, auto-update wiring (#7, #8, #10, #11)\n\nReal gaps found (not assumptions):\n- build/entitlements.mac.plist was REFERENCED in package.json (mac.entitlements /\n  entitlementsInherit) but did not exist — package:mac would have failed.\n  Added: audio-input + screen-recording entitlements (mic + system-audio loopback\n  capture, matching what main.ts''s getUserMedia/desktopCapturer flow needs under\n  Hardened Runtime), plus the standard Hardened Runtime JIT/unsigned-memory set.\n- electron-updater was already a dependency (and build.publish already pointed at\n  GitHub Releases) but had zero call sites anywhere in the codebase — #11 was\n  entirely unwired. Added electron/services/auto-update.ts:\n  checkForUpdatesAndNotify() on app ready, no-op outside app.isPackaged so\n  `npm run dev` never touches GitHub Releases.\n- Linux target added `rpm` (#10 asked for AppImage + .deb + .rpm; only the first\n  two were configured) and a desktop-entry name/comment override.\n- mac target added `pkg` (#7 asks for \"DMG + .pkg target\"; only dmg+zip were\n  configured — zip is kept, electron-updater''s mac autoUpdater requires it).\n\n## What I verified vs. did not\n- `npm run typecheck / lint / test (124/124) / build` — all clean.\n- `npx electron-builder --linux --dir` and `--win --dir`: caught and fixed a\n  REAL schema bug (linux.desktop must be `{ entry: {...} }`, not a flat object —\n  v26 rejected the flat form outright). Both then got as far as downloading\n  Electron and starting to unpack it, but failed with `EPERM: operation not\n  permitted, rename ... .tmp -> ...` in this sandbox — a filesystem-permission\n  limitation of this execution environment, not a config error (same failure,\n  same step, on both platform targets). Could not produce or inspect an actual\n  packaged artifact here.\n- Did NOT verify: actual code signing (no certificates available — #7/#8''s own\n  text already calls this \"Operator action\"), actual notarization (needs real\n  Apple ID/app-specific-password/team-ID env vars), actual auto-update runtime\n  behavior (needs a real published GitHub Release to update against).\n\n## Explicitly out of scope here\nSnap/Flatpak (#10 itself defers these to \"ileri faz\"). Staged rollout\npercentage (5%->25%->100%) is release-metadata electron-builder writes into\nlatest*.yml at publish time, not application code — nothing to wire beyond the\nupdate-check call already added.\n\n* fix(packaging): ship runtime resources and mac privacy metadata\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"80e5ae1c7bb8d9b6f0c38dec9b1c8cc3b7a53dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/80e5ae1c7bb8d9b6f0c38dec9b1c8cc3b7a53dd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f","verification":{"payload":"tree 80e5ae1c7bb8d9b6f0c38dec9b1c8cc3b7a53dd6\nparent be8f94ef544b054938d49629c457f6af3faa9b3c\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1783672664 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783672664 +0300\n\nfeat(desktop): packaging groundwork — mac entitlements, linux rpm, auto-update wiring (#7, #8, #10, #11) (#36)\n\n* feat(desktop): packaging groundwork — mac entitlements, linux rpm/desktop-entry, auto-update wiring (#7, #8, #10, #11)\n\nReal gaps found (not assumptions):\n- build/entitlements.mac.plist was REFERENCED in package.json (mac.entitlements /\n  entitlementsInherit) but did not exist — package:mac would have failed.\n  Added: audio-input + screen-recording entitlements (mic + system-audio loopback\n  capture, matching what main.ts''s getUserMedia/desktopCapturer flow needs under\n  Hardened Runtime), plus the standard Hardened Runtime JIT/unsigned-memory set.\n- electron-updater was already a dependency (and build.publish already pointed at\n  GitHub Releases) but had zero call sites anywhere in the codebase — #11 was\n  entirely unwired. Added electron/services/auto-update.ts:\n  checkForUpdatesAndNotify() on app ready, no-op outside app.isPackaged so\n  `npm run dev` never touches GitHub Releases.\n- Linux target added `rpm` (#10 asked for AppImage + .deb + .rpm; only the first\n  two were configured) and a desktop-entry name/comment override.\n- mac target added `pkg` (#7 asks for \"DMG + .pkg target\"; only dmg+zip were\n  configured — zip is kept, electron-updater''s mac autoUpdater requires it).\n\n## What I verified vs. did not\n- `npm run typecheck / lint / test (124/124) / build` — all clean.\n- `npx electron-builder --linux --dir` and `--win --dir`: caught and fixed a\n  REAL schema bug (linux.desktop must be `{ entry: {...} }`, not a flat object —\n  v26 rejected the flat form outright). Both then got as far as downloading\n  Electron and starting to unpack it, but failed with `EPERM: operation not\n  permitted, rename ... .tmp -> ...` in this sandbox — a filesystem-permission\n  limitation of this execution environment, not a config error (same failure,\n  same step, on both platform targets). Could not produce or inspect an actual\n  packaged artifact here.\n- Did NOT verify: actual code signing (no certificates available — #7/#8''s own\n  text already calls this \"Operator action\"), actual notarization (needs real\n  Apple ID/app-specific-password/team-ID env vars), actual auto-update runtime\n  behavior (needs a real published GitHub Release to update against).\n\n## Explicitly out of scope here\nSnap/Flatpak (#10 itself defers these to \"ileri faz\"). Staged rollout\npercentage (5%->25%->100%) is release-metadata electron-builder writes into\nlatest*.yml at publish time, not application code — nothing to wire beyond the\nupdate-check call already added.\n\n* fix(packaging): ship runtime resources and mac privacy metadata\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUK9YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX6QQAGNy+MHAR0SUHFVb7/+ST79n\nz10AHjHKHBlHwSFUiCh+byN8T/QlHaHjvZ6Xsqd+5h2UCmq3V9r48eYSogWHF9jD\neRejxMG1OiR5DPAtVBi2bmcP