/api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/be8f94ef544b054938d49629c457f6af3faa9b3c"}],"sha":"3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/3036a9846e495c4db157fb81a5e79474bde3c24f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244165292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zeynep-serban","id":244165292,"login":"zeynep-serban","node_id":"U_kgDODo2qrA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/commits/be8f94ef544b054938d49629c457f6af3faa9b3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:15:38Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:15:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(desktop): system tray + notifications + auto-launch + window state (#6) (#35)\n\n* feat(desktop): system tray + notifications + auto-launch + window state (#6)\n\nScope delivered:\n- System tray icon with a recording-active indicator (separate active/idle\n  PNG); context menu: show window, stop the active recording, quit.\n- Native OS notifications (start/finish) — status only, no\n  transcript/audio content (KVKK).\n- Auto-launch on system startup via app.setLoginItemSettings (opt-in,\n  exposed through IPC for a future UI toggle; default unchanged).\n- Window size/position persistence (electron-store) with visibility\n  clamping so a window saved on a now-unplugged monitor doesn''t get\n  stranded off-screen; pure clamp logic is unit-tested independent of\n  Electron (window-bounds.ts / window-bounds.test.ts).\n- Closing the window now hides it to the tray instead of quitting, so an\n  active recording is not interrupted by an accidental close click; real\n  quit is the tray''s \"Çıkış\" item (or macOS Cmd+Q / dock quit).\n\nRenderer touches App.tsx only at the existing setRecording(true/false)\ncall sites, notifying the tray via window.electronAPI.tray.setRecordingActive\n— no change to the audio capture/session state machine itself.\n\nPlaceholder tray icons (public/icons/*.png) are generated, not designed —\nflagged for a real asset before production packaging.\n\nExplicitly NOT in this PR: \"pause/resume capture\" quick control from the\noriginal #6 scope. There is no pause/resume primitive anywhere in the\ncapture pipeline today (only start/chunk/finish/abort); adding one touches\nthe live recording state machine we spent today proving end-to-end, and\ndeserves its own focused change rather than being bundled here.\n\nValidation: npm run lint / typecheck / test (124/124) / build all clean.\n\n* fix(packaging): ship tray icons in packaged app\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"30239f6c8463c92ca66d3d81ee4a96d78c5ee1ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/trees/30239f6c8463c92ca66d3d81ee4a96d78c5ee1ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-desktop/git/commits/be8f94ef544b054938d49629c457f6af3faa9b3c","verification":{"payload":"tree 30239f6c8463c92ca66d3d81ee4a96d78c5ee1ea\nparent cad4d1fe65439c108116ddc3e154648c37b5de7f\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1783433738 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783433738 +0300\n\nfeat(desktop): system tray + notifications + auto-launch + window state (#6) (#35)\n\n* feat(desktop): system tray + notifications + auto-launch + window state (#6)\n\nScope delivered:\n- System tray icon with a recording-active indicator (separate active/idle\n  PNG); context menu: show window, stop the active recording, quit.\n- Native OS notifications (start/finish) — status only, no\n  transcript/audio content (KVKK).\n- Auto-launch on system startup via app.setLoginItemSettings (opt-in,\n  exposed through IPC for a future UI toggle; default unchanged).\n- Window size/position persistence (electron-store) with visibility\n  clamping so a window saved on a now-unplugged monitor doesn''t get\n  stranded off-screen; pure clamp logic is unit-tested independent of\n  Electron (window-bounds.ts / window-bounds.test.ts).\n- Closing the window now hides it to the tray instead of quitting, so an\n  active recording is not interrupted by an accidental close click; real\n  quit is the tray''s \"Çıkış\" item (or macOS Cmd+Q / dock quit).\n\nRenderer touches App.tsx only at the existing setRecording(true/false)\ncall sites, notifying the tray via window.electronAPI.tray.setRecordingActive\n— no change to the audio capture/session state machine itself.\n\nPlaceholder tray icons (public/icons/*.png) are generated, not designed —\nflagged for a real asset before production packaging.\n\nExplicitly NOT in this PR: \"pause/resume capture\" quick control from the\noriginal #6 scope. There is no pause/resume primitive anywhere in the\ncapture pipeline today (only start/chunk/finish/abort); adding one touches\nthe live recording state machine we spent today proving end-to-end, and\ndeserves its own focused change rather than being bundled here.\n\nValidation: npm run lint / typecheck / test (124/124) / build all clean.\n\n* fix(packaging): ship tray icons in packaged app\n\n