ubscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-mobile/commit/2e6a04630d3c9d3d2706d4d8266c43ed1273e0ad","node_id":"C_kwDOSvTj09oAKDJlNmEwNDYzMGQzYzlkM2QyNzA2ZDRkODI2NmM0M2VkMTI3M2UwYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-mobile/commit/03e7003785299681844e2d32a9f72865e7d0d928","sha":"03e7003785299681844e2d32a9f72865e7d0d928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-mobile/commits/03e7003785299681844e2d32a9f72865e7d0d928"}],"sha":"2e6a04630d3c9d3d2706d4d8266c43ed1273e0ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-mobile/commits/2e6a04630d3c9d3d2706d4d8266c43ed1273e0ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-mobile/commits/03e7003785299681844e2d32a9f72865e7d0d928/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T00:46:48Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T00:46:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(e2e): Maestro + Detox scaffold + workflow + strategy doc (Faz 24 M6) (#14)\n\nTwo-track mobile E2E per issue #1 — Maestro as the primary flow track\n(fast, declarative, Expo-Go friendly) and Detox wired for the deep\nnative cases (permissions, background/foreground, WebSocket reconnect)\nthat outgrow YAML flows. Rationale + when-to-use in docs/e2e-strategy.md.\n\nLanding in this PR:\n\n- .maestro/config.yaml + .maestro/flows/01-app-launch.yaml\n    Working smoke flow that launches the app, asserts on `app-root` and\n    `meeting-list-header` testIDs, and takes a screenshot. Fails loudly\n    when a testID is missing — that IS the signal for the renderer to\n    add it (İ-M2 in the roadmap).\n\n- .detoxrc.js + e2e/jest.config.js + e2e/app-launch.test.ts\n    Detox config for iOS sim + Android emu, plus a spec skeleton that\n    mirrors the Maestro smoke. NOT wired in CI until the Expo prebuild\n    is committed (managed workflow needs `expo prebuild` + `eas build\n    --profile development` to produce the native binaries Detox\n    consumes). Running `npm run test:e2e:ios` locally works today\n    after the prebuild.\n\n- .github/workflows/e2e-mobile.yml\n    workflow_dispatch trigger + pull_request path filter. Includes a\n    fail-loud stub so a dispatch without a runner does not silently\n    pass, and an ubuntu-hosted `stub-until-runner` job that runs on\n    PRs to document the local command so a PR touching E2E surfaces\n    still gets a green baseline in the Checks tab.\n\n- docs/e2e-strategy.md\n    Framework choice + when-to-reach-for-which + runner options\n    (self-hosted mac / BrowserStack / local-only) + 5-step roadmap\n    from scaffold → wired CI → SSE flow coverage.\n\nSequencing (roadmap):\n  İ-M1 (this PR)  scaffold + workflow + docs\n  İ-M2            wire `app-root` + `meeting-list-header` testIDs in\n                  the renderer → Maestro smoke first green\n  İ-M3            login (Keycloak PKCE) + meeting-list happy path\n                  (Maestro) + native permission flow (Detox)\n  İ-M4            runner decision + CI enable\n  İ-M5            Faz 24 canlı analiz SSE consumer flow (Maestro)\n                  + reconnect flow (Detox)\n\nZero renderer changes in this PR — everything is pre-work so the app\nside stays completely stable. When `app-root` testID lands, Maestro\nsmoke flips green with no scaffold rework.\n\nRef: platform-mobile#1 (board), HARD RULE — Tarayıcıdan Sonuç\nDoğrulanmadan İş Bitmedi (browser MCP mobile için yetmez).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0c962800a9c6c09aa2e1938ea8c1fbbd21c2202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-mobile/git/trees/f0c962800a9c6c09aa2e1938ea8c1fbbd21c2202"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-mobile/git/commits/03e7003785299681844e2d32a9f72865e7d0d928","verification":{"payload":"tree f0c962800a9c6c09aa2e1938ea8c1fbbd21c2202\nparent 3a609a839f7ea8cc4a3f6dfd115f80c1d4417ee6\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1784594808 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784594808 +0300\n\nfeat(e2e): Maestro + Detox scaffold + workflow + strategy doc (Faz 24 M6) (#14)\n\nTwo-track mobile E2E per issue #1 — Maestro as the primary flow track\n(fast, declarative, Expo-Go friendly) and Detox wired for the deep\nnative cases (permissions, background/foreground, WebSocket reconnect)\nthat outgrow YAML flows. Rationale + when-to-use in docs/e2e-strategy.md.\n\nLanding in this PR:\n\n- .maestro/config.yaml + .maestro/flows/01-app-launch.yaml\n    Working smoke flow that launches the app, asserts on `app-root` and\n    `meeting-list-header` testIDs, and takes a screenshot. Fails loudly\n    when a testID is missing — that IS the signal for the renderer to\n    add it (İ-M2 in the roadmap).\n\n- .detoxrc.js + e2e/jest.config.js + e2e/app-launch.test.ts\n    Detox config for iOS sim + Android emu, plus a spec skeleton that\n    mirrors the Maestro smoke. NOT wired in CI until the Expo prebuild\n    is committed (managed workflow needs `expo prebuild` + `eas build\n    --profile development` to produce the native binaries Detox\n    consumes). Running `npm run test:e2e:ios` locally works today\n    after the prebuild.\n\n- .github/workflows/e2e-mobile.yml\n    workflow_dispatch trigger + pull_request path filter. Includes a\n    fail-loud stub so a dispatch without a runner does not silently\n    pass, and an ubuntu-hosted `stub-until-runner` job that runs on\n    PRs to document the local command so a PR touching E2E surfaces\n    still gets a green baseline in the Checks tab.\n\n- docs/e2e-strategy.md\n    Framework choice + when-to-reach-for-which + runner options\n    (self-hosted mac / BrowserStack / local-only) + 5-step roadmap\n    from scaffold → wired CI → SSE flow coverage.\n\nSequencing (roadmap):\n  İ-M1 (this PR)  scaffold + workflow + docs\n  İ-M2            wire `app-root` + `meeting-list-header` testIDs in\n                  the renderer → Maestro smoke first green\n  İ-M3            login (Keycloak PKCE) + meeting-list happy path\n                  (Maestro) + native permission flow (Detox)\n  İ-M4            runner decision + CI enable\n  İ-M5            Faz 24 canlı analiz SSE consumer flow (Maestro)\n                  + reconnect flow (Detox)\n\nZero renderer changes in this PR — everything is pre-work so the app\nside stays completely stable. When `app-root` testID lands, Maestro\nsmoke flips green with no scaffold rework.\n\nRef: platform-mobile#1 (board), HARD RULE — Tarayıcıdan Sonuç\nDoğrulanmadan İş Bitmedi (browser MCP mobile için yetmez).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXsF4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8a4QAIqzqZBYF+3u5ag6mcz3vrW8\nrMvjboWu2Kli6tC4UBxkvYbHfZ1p37r/pKabed/GztgJcnIseBgnp+08SZ8qw2c3\nVnVqzuofbZOlKzPBWdfumcWtUDGk3aTdusyLTzfP/L0gWWpNjmJDlwHav7JrL88m\nw5Kv9RXu9VuyuJ+6k2IiWwa/9wbTCwOtNj44qk3b6OXMlutfDIT/MJtiRB