mail":"eheva87@gmail.com","name":"vitali87"},"message":"fix(realtime): handle non-code files and filter spurious events\n\nThis commit fixes three issues in the real-time file watcher:\n\n1. Filter spurious file system events: Only process MODIFIED, CREATED,\n   and deleted events. Previously, read-only events like \"opened\" and\n   \"closed_no_write\" (triggered by IDEs accessing files) would cause\n   files to be deleted from the graph but not recreated, since Step 3\n   only runs for modification events.\n\n2. Delete File nodes for non-code files: The existing CYPHER_DELETE_MODULE\n   query only deletes Module nodes (for code files). Added a separate\n   query to delete File nodes, ensuring non-code files like .md, .json,\n   etc. are properly removed when deleted from the filesystem.\n\n3. Create File nodes for ALL file types: Added process_generic_file()\n   call for all files during MODIFIED/CREATED events, not just code\n   files with recognized language configs. This ensures non-code files\n   are indexed in real-time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"930f77dab48dba0501a74f92a5a2c96102f3000b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyanpen/code-graph-rag/git/trees/930f77dab48dba0501a74f92a5a2c96102f3000b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyanpen/code-graph-rag/git/commits/c1e719a766a475598af5ebbd7f09c9d4b3432d00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22404335?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitali87/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitali87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitali87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitali87/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vitali87","id":22404335,"login":"vitali87","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDA0MzM1","organizations_url":