comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T19:28:15Z","email":"170351+djbender@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Derek Bender"},"message":"Adopt FDS manifest schema with client-side traffic splitting and canary KPI deploy\n\n- Rewrite discovery.local.json to AWS Frontend Discovery Service shape: schema URL,\n  microFrontends keyed by name, each holding a version array with deployment.traffic\n  and deployment.default; widget-kpi demonstrates a 90/10 split across two live servers\n- Shell consumes FDS manifest natively: selectVersion() picks a version per widget via\n  djb2 hash bucketing; ?token=default forces bucket 1, ?token=canary forces bucket 100;\n  version-scoped remoteName (widget-kpi_1_0_0 / widget-kpi_1_1_0) prevents MF runtime\n  cache collisions when both versions run simultaneously; bucket chip uses same hash\n  inputs as selectVersion so displayed bucket always matches the selected version cohort\n- Replace widget-kpi vite.config.js with vite.config.v1-0-0.js and vite.config.v1-1-0.js,\n  each hardcoding port, federation name, version, and outDir; bin/dev passes --config to\n  each; use import.meta.env.VITE_WIDGET_VERSION instead of define/__WIDGET_VERSION__\n  because Vite''s define is skipped when React Fast Refresh runs, causing HMR re-transforms\n  to produce the wrong version\n- validateManifest requires deployment.traffic and deployment.default on every entry;\n  validates traffic percentages sum to 100 for multi-version widgets\n- Add port 5002 webServer entry to playwright.config.js; add preview/preview:v1-1-0\n  scripts to widget-kpi package.json with versioned --config flags; set global test\n  timeout to 1000ms and remove per-assertion timeout overrides from all e2e specs\n- Add traffic splitting explainer section to footer and README","tree":{"sha":"78bf6271b85f002602243b1084027fe5373eb2b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djbender/micro-frontends-demo/git/trees/78bf6271b85f002602243b1084027fe5373eb2b8"},"url":"https://api.github.c