"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/b6a4679aad8028791e152350b9bd1ef6889cec01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T18:04:29Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T18:04:29Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"refactor: remove internal quality-target vocabulary from public surfaces\n\nOwner directive (all projects): terms like \"SOTA\", \"state-of-the-art\" and\n\"world class\" are internal quality targets, never outward-facing claims —\nnothing tracked (code, tests, public docs) may carry them.\n\n- tools/validate_sota_evidence_ledger.py -> validate_claim_evidence_ledger.py\n  (with its test): the gate validates evidence behind public performance\n  claims, so it is named by content; ledger state \"sota_gate_passed\" ->\n  \"claim_gate_passed\"; the internal gitignored ledger moves to\n  docs/internal/claim_evidence_ledger.json (migrated locally).\n- FAIR bundle: gate key internal_sota_ledger -> internal_claim_ledger,\n  label and claim-boundary text now say \"performance-superiority claim\";\n  bundle and capability artifacts regenerated.\n- ADR 0010 / merge-window features doc / external-sources index: study and\n  citation context renamed descriptively (competitive-trajectory study,\n  comparative latency context).\n- pyproject: mutation-pilot comment loses its campaign label.\n\nInternal gitignored docs (docs/internal/, session logs) keep the vocabulary\n- that is where the targets live. The PR template and CONTRIBUTING rules\nthat forbid quality labels stay as guards.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"5628b4d5a6a7f5e8daacddc01499efed7c39a9dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/trees/5628b4d5a6a7f5e8daacddc01499efed7c39a9dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/commits/b6a4679aad8028791e152350b9bd1ef6889cec01","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/b6a4679aad8028791e152350b9bd1ef6889cec01","node_id":"C_kwDOSwL0LtoAKGI2YTQ2NzlhYWQ4MDI4NzkxZTE1MjM1MGI5YmQxZWY2ODg5Y2VjMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/beeb2e7b4bdc615d37c1e704fdd46d78d4f86dbf","sha":"beeb2e7b4bdc615d37c1e704fdd46d78d4f86dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/beeb2e7b4bdc615d37c1e704fdd46d78d4f86dbf"}],"sha":"b6a4679aad8028791e152350b9bd1ef6889cec01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/b6a4679aad8028791e152350b9bd1ef6889cec01"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/beeb2e7b4bdc615d37c1e704fdd46d78d4f86dbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T12:04:24Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T12:04:24Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(lifecycle): rayon-parallel independently seeded merger campaigns\n\nSOTA-10 A5 (plan Pillar A). The MIF-012 verification campaigns gain an\nindependently seeded lane: verify_merger_boundedness_seeded /\nverify_merger_liveness_seeded derive one generator per trial (the\nseed ^ ((trial+1) * mix) SplitMix64 convention shared with the MIF-017\nstress injector) instead of threading a single generator through every\ntrial, so the campaign is invariant to trial execution order. That\ninvariance is what the new Rust rayon lane exploits: the parallel, the\nRust sequential, and the Python reference produce BIT-IDENTICAL reports\n(whole-report parity incl. failure strings asserted across budgets, seeds,\nand the failure path; the execution-order-invariance contract is pinned as\ncampaign == fold-of-standalone-trials). The original shared-stream\nverifiers stay unchanged as their own documented contract.\n\nMeasured at the default budgets (taskset 4 cores, moderate load — honest\ncontext in the promoted JSON): boundedness 100x500 5.66 ms vs 588 ms\nmedian, liveness 1000x200 0.69 ms vs 75.6 ms — about two orders of\nmagnitude, dispatched rust-first as lifecycle.merger_campaign.\n\nSingle sequence: dispatched factories + python-floor fallback test,\ntop-level re-exports (191), FFI pyfunctions, 25 new tests (100% branch on\nthe extended module incl. the injected broken-marking failure path), bench\nharness + promoted JSON, dispatch registration, docs section, dashboard\nnow 19 kernels / 34 groups, all six drift gates green (FAIR last).\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"fe22efeeeda8c850ab29f04546056623cc0fb584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/trees/fe22efeeeda8c850ab29f04546056623cc0fb584"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/commits/beeb2e7b4bdc615d37c1e704fdd46d78d4f86dbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/