ublic"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/aa67b0aabdf8a244d7ac29a3031cd8c16302d552/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T02:02:41Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T02:02:41Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"build(deps): bump github/codeql-action to v4.36.3 across all four actions\n\nDependabot opened four separate PRs (init, autobuild, analyze,\nupload-sarif), each bumping one action in isolation; CodeQL rejects mixed\nversions (\"Loaded a configuration file for version ''4.36.2'', but running\nversion ''4.36.3''\"), so three of the four PRs fail their own CI by\nconstruction. Bumping all four references together in one commit keeps the\ninit/analyze pair consistent; the Dependabot PRs then close as satisfied.\n\nVerified: https://api.github.com/repos/github/codeql-action/git/ref/tags/v4.36.3\n(annotated tag 8533807f dereferences to commit 54f647b7, the pinned SHA)\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"3d097d8e8f6dbfca51496ba939c23715a554346f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/trees/3d097d8e8f6dbfca51496ba939c23715a554346f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/commits/aa67b0aabdf8a244d7ac29a3031cd8c16302d552","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/aa67b0aabdf8a244d7ac29a3031cd8c16302d552","node_id":"C_kwDOSwL0LtoAKGFhNjdiMGFhYmRmOGEyNDRkN2FjMjlhMzAzMWNkOGMxNjMwMmQ1NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d","sha":"4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d"}],"sha":"aa67b0aabdf8a244d7ac29a3031cd8c16302d552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/aa67b0aabdf8a244d7ac29a3031cd8c16302d552"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T01:30:05Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T01:30:05Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(kinematic): opt-in fire-time selection with first-lock default\n\nSOTA-12 B3. New kinematic.fire_time: retrospective fire-instant selection\nover an evaluated merge-window trace. FIRST_LOCK (default) reproduces the\nstreaming trigger''s latch instant — pinned against the actual streaming\nengine; MAX_WINDOW_MARGIN (opt-in) picks the locked sample with the widest\nnormalised window margin min((phi_tol-phi_err)/phi_tol,\n(x_tol-x_ref)/x_tol), ties to the earliest sample.\n\nSubordinate by construction: selection only among samples the deterministic\nmerge-window law already locked, and only when the MIF-011 batch safety\ncertificate passed, the bank is feasible, and the lane is armed. The policy\ncan change when an admissible shot fires, never whether an inadmissible one\ndoes — every blocking gate and a 50-trace seeded subordination sweep are\npinned in tests (100% branch). Like the merge-window feature boundary and\nthe advisory predictor, this is once-per-shot selection logic with no\nmulti-language acceleration path (documented).\n\nTop-level re-exports (187 exports), docs page + mkdocs nav, capability and\nFAIR artifacts regenerated and drift-gated.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"f3115a9a0fa11fe7e55de828bb700086e9f929d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/trees/f3115a9a0fa11fe7e55de828bb700086e9f929d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/commits/4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d","node_id":"C_kwDOSwL0LtoAKDRkOTZjN2EzMjNhYTcyMTE5ZTYyNzIyYjU5ODUzYTkwNTEwOTNlMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commit/8ffe3574912f63569249f9034ee5507df19c86d5","sha":"8ffe3574912f63569249f9034ee5507df19c86d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/8ffe3574912f63569249f9034ee5507df19c86d5"}],"sha":"4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/4d96c7a323aa72119e62722b59853a9051093e1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/commits/8ffe3574912f63569249f9034ee5507df19c86d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T01:22:10Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T01:22:10Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(kinematic): probabilistic lock/abort propagation for the merge trigger\n\nSOTA-12 B1. New kinematic.trigger_probability: per-sample P(lock) and\nP(envelope violation) propagated analytically from the MIF-017\nadditive-Gaussian sensor noise model through the MIF-003 merge-window\ndecision law and the MIF-011 sampled safety envelope, giving the trigger a\nstated FIRE/ABORT_UNSAFE/HOLD operating point (false-fire and missed-window\nrates) instead of bare thresholds.\n\n- Exact forward recursion over the consecutive-streak Markov states\n  (pinned against brute-force enumeration over all candidate sequences);\n  per-step envelope hazards from the one-step slack distribution\n  N(slack_k, sigma_s^2*(1+c^2)); cumulative violation under a documented\n  independence approximation; sigma=0 collapses to the exact monitor and\n  certificate indicators (pinned against the production surfaces).\n- Deterministic Monte-Carlo calibration tests against the real MIF-017\n  DegradedSensorStream engine (2500 fixed-seed campaigns; 4-binomial-SE\n  tolerance; documented 0.05 bound on the cumulative approximation).\n- Rust mirror (mif-kinematic trigger_probability, erfc via libm 0.2 —\n  rust-lang crate, no_std) with bit-exact parity asserted with no\n  tolerance across noiseless, mid-range, deep-tail, and boundary fixtures.\n- Zero-copy FFI column boundary (read-only NumPy views in, probability\n  columns out as NumPy arrays): the per-sample tuple boundary was measured\n  first and lost the 4096-sample group to object conversion (134 ms vs\n  70 ms median); with columns Rust wins both groups (135 us vs 308 us on\n  the 64-sample per-shot call, 16.0 ms vs 22.2 ms on 4096) and\n  kinematic.trigger_probability dispatches rust-first.\n- dispatched_trigger_probabilities + python-floor fallback test; top-level\n  re-exports (183 exports); docs page + mkdocs nav; benchmark JSON promoted\n  with full provenance; all six generated artifacts regenerated and\n  drift-gated (dashboard now 18 kernels / 32 groups).\n\nVerified: https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/libm\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"8690eb3f2375cae9d6639d0dd1d5dcc3eefb3530","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/trees/8690eb3f2375cae9d6639d0dd1d5dcc3eefb3530"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-mif-core/git/commits/8ffe3574912f63569249f9034ee5507df19c86d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"http