ions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/andregs/lean-dev-br/commit/d62f237b104730b38b7fb11675b1211c216f7d92","node_id":"C_kwDOSwhTatoAKGQ2MmYyMzdiMTA0NzMwYjM4YjdmYjExNjc1YjEyMTFjMjE2ZjdkOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/andregs/lean-dev-br/commit/8b5f5a9a8c1696fe1ea67ceb4c6fa084ae1639b2","sha":"8b5f5a9a8c1696fe1ea67ceb4c6fa084ae1639b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/8b5f5a9a8c1696fe1ea67ceb4c6fa084ae1639b2"}],"sha":"d62f237b104730b38b7fb11675b1211c216f7d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/d62f237b104730b38b7fb11675b1211c216f7d92"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/712092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andregs","id":712092,"login":"andregs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjA5Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/8b5f5a9a8c1696fe1ea67ceb4c6fa084ae1639b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T02:11:12Z","email":"andregs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"André Gomes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T02:11:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(wanderlust): BFF + end-to-end wiring (#42)\n\n* fix(wanderlust-contracts): correct Problem schema to real RFC 7807 shape\n\ntype isn''t required (Spring''s ProblemDetail omits the about:blank\ndefault), and instance is a URI-reference, not a full URI - found by\nwriting a conformance test that validates real responses against the\nspec.\n\n* ci(wanderlust-contracts): gate on openapi.yaml/schema.d.ts drift\n\nNew openapi-types-check target regenerates schema.d.ts and diffs it\nagainst the committed copy - catches a spec edit that forgot to\nregenerate types, wired into the affected task list in ci.yml.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-bff): REST pass-through to catalog\n\nRestCatalogClient (RestClient, native runtime hints for Destination/\nWeather) behind a CatalogClient seam meant to be swapped for a gRPC\nclient in iteration 2. DestinationController maps upstream 404/\nunavailable to RFC 7807 problem+json. OTel wiring mirrors relay-service\n(DirectOtlpTracingConfig, JUL bridge).\n\n* test(wanderlust-bff): cover controller and RestCatalogClient\n\nPlain unit test for the controller, @WebMvcTest for real HTTP status/\ncontent-type (problem+json on 404/502), and a local HttpServer-backed\ntest for RestCatalogClient''s success/404/failure mapping.\n\n* test(wanderlust-bff,wanderlust-catalog): enforce openapi.yaml conformance\n\ncom.atlassian.oai:openapi-request-validator-mockmvc validates real\nDestinationController responses (200s and problem+json errors) against\nlibs/wanderlust-contracts'' spec, read by relative path rather than\nduplicated. Backend still hand-writes DTOs (openapi-generator codegen\nretrofit deferred to iteration 2 - see project_wanderlust_k8s_showcase\nmemory), so this is what stands in for contract enforcement on the API\nside until then.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-web): gate MSW behind env + add backend proxy config\n\nenvironment.mswEnabled defaults true (dev/e2e/static build unaffected).\nNew `backend` serve configuration flips it off via fileReplacement and\nproxies /api to a real wanderlust-bff (proxy.conf.json), for exercising\nthe actual Angular -> BFF -> catalog chain locally.","tree":{"sha":"d2d360e2be92481c50468a5fa74e5a5039b43333","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/trees/d2d360e2be92481c50468a5fa74e5a5039b43333"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/commits/8b5f5a9a8c1696fe1ea67ceb4c6fa084ae1639b2","verification":{"payload":"tree d2d360e2be92481c50468a5fa74e5a5039b43333\nparent dc8e4f445e825d3eb1ceabf0e4d6aefae637a043\nauthor André Gomes <andregs@users.noreply.github.com> 1783822272 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783822272 +0000\n\nfeat(wanderlust): BFF + end-to-end wiring (#42)\n\n* fix(wanderlust-contracts): correct Problem schema to real RFC 7807 shape\n\ntype isn''t required (Spring''s ProblemDetail omits the about:blank\ndefault), and instance is a URI-reference, not a full URI - found by\nwriting a conformance test that validates real responses against the\nspec.\n\n* ci(wanderlust-contracts): gate on openapi.yaml/schema.d.ts drift\n\nNew openapi-types-check target regenerates schema.d.ts and diffs it\nagainst the committed copy - catches a spec edit that forgot to\nregenerate types, wired into the affected task list in ci.yml.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-bff): REST pass-through to catalog\n\nRestCatalogClient (RestClient, native runtime hints for Destination/\nWeather) behind a CatalogClient seam meant to be swapped for a gRPC\nclient in iteration 2. DestinationController maps upstream 404/\nunavailable to RFC 7807 problem+json. OTel wiring mirrors relay-service\n(DirectOtlpTracingConfig, JUL bridge).\n\n* test(wanderlust-bff): cover controller and RestCatalogClient\n\nPlain unit test for the controller, @WebMvcTest for real HTTP status/\ncontent-type (problem+json on 404/502), and a local HttpServer-backed\ntest for RestCatalogClient''s success/404/failure mapping.\n\n* test(wanderlust-bff,wanderlust-catalog): enforce openapi.yaml conformance\n\ncom.atlassian.oai:openapi-request-validator-mockmvc validates real\nDestinationController responses (200s and problem+json errors) against\nlibs/wanderlust-contracts'' spec, read by relative path rather than\nduplicated. Backend still hand-writes DTOs (openapi-generator codegen\nretrofit deferred to iteration 2 - see project_wanderlust_k8s_showcase\nmemory), so this is what stands in for contract enforcement on the API\nside until then.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-web): gate MSW behind env + add backend proxy config\n\nenvironment.mswEnabled defaults true (dev/e2e/static build unaffected).\nNew `backend` serve configuration flips it off via fileReplacement and\nproxies /api to a real wanderlust-bff (proxy.conf.json), for exercising\nthe actual Angular -> BFF -> catalog chain locally.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUvfACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHHYQAG15UOQNfLZefnPCToRI7am2\nQeJNS7+UsQ0GMKRzEWXVyM8UNU4r3nihigmnBbKwF1uwJsXsJcphR0KnMvayJctm\nCRxfNL84iZkBzTDXgeLRXU0+wR/uF7u3+dMbSL2oBD2qppB2SaoPGQEHaICaqKgU\nwOjwtU0uQPLfxuI+WcEGU5DdNL3Qg0LppyS55cWKF46Yw8rxwkZJ3P+6T2GMpBdn\nHKQ9ry7oSwKme0HVQ+Ro10blwYtTlCsxIXWlMj3cYe8f3GjAAgM3CwHXCDhKMK+k\nvHmbTrKu+B+jRqJt70IFzwI/bVZZVX+v8SFDjldMrfxUd9Q8uhiVCFn6OybTFKAb\ncHW01KX0yXZcXfuMuevSqmL5YwERyTyE7HR+kKf/zEkpXn3sNr/8JKgAuCV+UqxO\n/RFbx+XiuVToFKqRGBZ0Wm4s05OhlEUTtt8Q9sj2C+XhxOUjJZMy3DrZoEanXYn8\nxqVZgQgNys2lR/vJVHHtXdrsSxK3CpHYGAkoJAU7FqFhiYd3okK08/aGtrLiOA2Z\nC6qapYf8rWpyFZlck6hljhCs7THAUn12K+Pdyqk7Laz4dV6qq/hvZSx5cZncO/TQ\nueSEofFF6BF2e3m7Xyn9bpXsglqu3iI7n1paGzcZMHaviMu4vwIIakVTIjjgoPZB\n5EFFLa/DMMSMUAZmph2c\n=yLHy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T02:11:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.g