","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/cd74e71b6711d9bef9e6e8554f98cd44512b3066/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T02:24:54Z","email":"andregs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"André Gomes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T02:24:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(wanderlust-catalog): exclude Valkey from readiness, poll it in CI (#39)\n\n* fix(wanderlust-catalog): exclude Valkey from the readiness health group\n\nWeatherCache already degrades gracefully on a Redis outage, but the\nauto-configured Redis health indicator was still failing the\naggregate /actuator/health — caught by CI''s native-smoke, which has\nno Valkey. Redis stays in the default aggregate (visible to\ndashboards) but is excluded from readiness, so a cache-only outage\ndoesn''t block a rollout.\n\n* ci: native-smoke polls /actuator/health/readiness, not the bare endpoint\n\nMirrors the actual k8s readinessProbe this stands in for, and\ncorrectly ignores degraded-but-functional dependencies an app\nalready handles gracefully (e.g. wanderlust-catalog''s Valkey cache).\nConfirmed available by default on relay-service too, no extra\nper-service config needed.\n\n* ci: dedupe push+pull_request runs for the same commit\n\nOnce a PR exists, every push ran the full workflow twice (push +\npull_request events for the same commit) — native-build is the\nexpensive part now. concurrency group keyed by the shared commit\nsha cancels the redundant run instead of both completing.","tree":{"sha":"5bbdfc35e2d8c75e76046b3bdadc370227fb7dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/trees/5bbdfc35e2d8c75e76046b3bdadc370227fb7dd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/commits/cd74e71b6711d9bef9e6e8554f98cd44512b3066","verification":{"payload":"tree 5bbdfc35e2d8c75e76046b3bdadc370227fb7dd1\nparent 92a7de018a57021f08c523e6e46b1eeda02b640d\nauthor André Gomes <andregs@users.noreply.github.com> 1783736694 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783736694 -0300\n\nfix(wanderlust-catalog): exclude Valkey from readiness, poll it in CI (#39)\n\n* fix(wanderlust-catalog): exclude Valkey from the readiness health group\n\nWeatherCache already degrades gracefully on a Redis outage, but the\nauto-configured Redis health indicator was still failing the\naggregate /actuator/health — caught by CI''s native-smoke, which has\nno Valkey. Redis stays in the default aggregate (visible to\ndashboards) but is excluded from readiness, so a cache-only outage\ndoesn''t block a rollout.\n\n* ci: native-smoke polls /actuator/health/readiness, not the bare endpoint\n\nMirrors the actual k8s readinessProbe this stands in for, and\ncorrectly ignores degraded-but-functional dependencies an app\nalready handles gracefully (e.g. wanderlust-catalog''s Valkey cache).\nConfirmed available by default on relay-service too, no extra\nper-service config needed.\n\n* ci: dedupe push+pull_request runs for the same commit\n\nOnce a PR exists, every push ran the full workflow twice (push +\npull_request events for the same commit) — native-build is the\nexpensive part now. concurrency group keyed by the shared commit\nsha cancels the redundant run instead of both completing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUal2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc80QAFXM7kgbk2ciRGnulWMehY3N\n/quJ+vpMNlFeK4ndv3DmtalitCtb2VSD8zfnVohFf0VGcOOfbE2AtF/+l89FDtpC\nVDVY3O6gmUkrZ+qd0uN7my3/6xZ5Umv2AWr3iRPCbfeq+8kIzoVfay7AQkyTd9KI\nta7mO36ptS6XOHmVoo1LHJV8tn9XBK4sUITpbuFSiUlIgKwH4ND4zqp4jNjtYiWF\nHzJ+2oK7MDRLvp46r+lt8ifN+rlwcd8M5Vgiqtb8rvMaDBE1+CCww9rwfIbk3TFH\n2xy8LFiPT0qCO3