":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/andregs/lean-dev-br/commit/ee8b20d1bbd52ef810d9afe7d2816510e8de19f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSwhTatoAKGVlOGIyMGQxYmJkNTJlZjgxMGQ5YWZlN2QyODE2NTEwZThkZTE5ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/andregs/lean-dev-br/commit/aa19274d2ce7e2096086c038bf286fe58e4ab3f6","sha":"aa19274d2ce7e2096086c038bf286fe58e4ab3f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/aa19274d2ce7e2096086c038bf286fe58e4ab3f6"}],"sha":"ee8b20d1bbd52ef810d9afe7d2816510e8de19f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/ee8b20d1bbd52ef810d9afe7d2816510e8de19f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/712092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andregs","id":712092,"login":"andregs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjA5Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/aa19274d2ce7e2096086c038bf286fe58e4ab3f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:23:11Z","email":"andregs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"André Gomes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:23:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(wanderlust): catalog destinations endpoint, naive N+1 weather (#36)\n\n* build(wanderlust-catalog): add opentelemetry + openfeature deps\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): weather config + OTel tracing wiring\n\nCatalogProperties externalizes the Open-Meteo endpoint/timeouts and\nthe flags-source URL. DirectOtlpTracingConfig mirrors relay-service''s\nunconditional BatchSpanProcessor bean (Spring''s own is gated on\n@ConditionalOnProperty, which native AOT bakes in at build time —\nour OTLP endpoint is a runtime env var).\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): OpenFeature client over flagd-schema flags.json\n\nSame flags.json the JS apps read via @openfeature/*-sdk. Falls back\nto a bundled copy when unreachable (offline local dev). flagd daemon\nreplaces the InMemoryProvider later with no app-code change.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): Open-Meteo weather client, naive per-call path\n\nOne HTTP call per destination for now; batching lands with the\nValkey cache in a follow-up PR. Any upstream failure degrades to a\nnull weather rather than failing the request.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): destinations endpoint, naive N+1 weather fan-out\n\nGET /destinations and /destinations/{id} aggregate weather per\ndestination via WeatherService — one Open-Meteo call per\ndestination. RFC7807 problem+json for unknown ids.\n\n* fix(wanderlust-catalog): register FlagsJson reflection for native image\n\nFlagsJson is deserialized by a manual RestClient call, never a\ncontroller type, so Spring''s AOT processing never discovers it and\nnative strips its record-accessor reflection. Native smoke run\ncrashed with UnsupportedFeatureError before this fix.\n\n* fix(wanderlust-catalog): register OpenMeteoResponse reflection for native image\n\nSame footgun as FlagsJson (previous commit): OpenMeteoResponse is\ndeserialized by a manual RestClient call, never a controller type.\nFull native smoke run (health + /destinations against real\nOpen-Meteo) now passes end-to-end.","tree":{"sha":"226e93bc151000062745055f5443ceabcb4fbded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/trees/226e93bc151000062745055f5443ceabcb4fbded"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/commits/aa19274d2ce7e2096086c038bf286fe58e4ab3f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 226e93bc151000062745055f5443ceabcb4fbded\nparent 045a9ea9e4717be21a7c15bc1ff92decaff4f630\nauthor André Gomes <andregs@users.noreply.github.com> 1783718591 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783718591 -0300\n\nfeat(wanderlust): catalog destinations endpoint, naive N+1 weather (#36)\n\n* build(wanderlust-catalog): add opentelemetry + openfeature deps\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): weather config + OTel tracing wiring\n\nCatalogProperties externalizes the Open-Meteo endpoint/timeouts and\nthe flags-source URL. DirectOtlpTracingConfig mirrors relay-service''s\nunconditional BatchSpanProcessor bean (Spring''s own is gated on\n@ConditionalOnProperty, which native AOT bakes in at build time —\nour OTLP endpoint is a runtime env var).\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): OpenFeature client over flagd-schema flags.json\n\nSame flags.json the JS apps read via @openfeature/*-sdk. Falls back\nto a bundled copy when unreachable (offline local dev). flagd daemon\nreplaces the InMemoryProvider later with no app-code change.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): Open-Meteo weather client, naive per-call path\n\nOne HTTP call per destination for now; batching lands with the\nValkey cache in a follow-up PR. Any upstream failure degrades to a\nnull weather rather than failing the request.\n\n* feat(wanderlust-catalog): destinations endpoint, naive N+1 weather fan-out\n\nGET /destinations and /destinations/{id} aggregate weather per\ndestination via WeatherService — one Open-Meteo call per\ndestination. RFC7807 problem+json for unknown ids.\n\n* fix(wanderlust-catalog): register FlagsJson reflection for native image\n\nFlagsJson is deserialized by a manual RestClient call, never a\ncontroller type, so Spring''s AOT processing never discovers it and\nnative strips its record-accessor reflection. Native smoke run\ncrashed with UnsupportedFeatureError before this fix.\n\n* fix(wanderlust-catalog): register OpenMeteoResponse reflection for native image\n\nSame footgun as FlagsJson (previous commit): OpenMeteoResponse is\ndeserialized by a manual RestClient call, never a controller type.\nFull native smoke run (health + /destinations against real\nOpen-Meteo) now passes end-to-end.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUWK/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWWUQAHHKUppUbXgyUAoFCdO9+gSJ\nz9+XmRLU29wN1Kfwol/36jhOw9FYSG7ZCW98siiytvAGIVTXVxRXkmYD5hC4ussL\ny/t+gOkWU/pdg06Lt/wGGlXW0wiH501+2u2ksQiYGASahTMkSsraj95wL8Yf3b5C\nXfJQ33zlC00NjwyOeSMxuEynqfc4VCUYgWbDuZa99kaQfVqo4RwABZHvzAT1vJqv\nV/96gke6fUZVGbluZfapFbf0SJUdwdzqTtxVHdrfotnE5NmNIgN4LhRrtx/Y0j/z\nmu6vERC8t+uX7kD3dBlA/AcBDMt++2fwMawJpTQIaEogARVSfiMaRSek2OaTSh+/\nQhfreo9OpN3ySXdIvHF7Qdy8ZjW6e1NmaD1RlAwVK7TcabJtgfFH5hUOwOC2oHjW\nZzfmMMKxtd+UAdA0Qxl+E09AZVZlozoS8MHoX7xWwKL70IgVnQYI1rRJLrmzBI+L\ncKPiczgLgBQ7r4CZV3z65SgJDzfGICM/wmHpV2suohyGuIxaRn1FD4aPps69Jak6\nYAvnVA2qiC1bws8En0Nx0aM1GlTpV/BDS+7YPS2ZK9wfqgxSV0BXDuEOhi5KWXek\n034k3tRYLFHzlvfpVqWvbwhDwRFBUh0necyX4dmoKm9DphvBwKKiGj+Sz6ZlKOK/\nvu5TCXQ0t5m3wKYbzdfE\n=xEhK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-10T21:23:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow