"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/1d832a783bb44e2e42fa21fd8dc82a590fa6846c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-04T03:01:08Z","email":"andregs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"André Gomes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-04T03:01:08Z","email":"andregs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"André Gomes"},"message":"fix(federation): build to app-local dist, not repo-root dist/apps\n\noutDir pointed at ../../dist/apps/federation-* (repo root) while\ninfra''s createSyncedFolder reads apps/federation-*/dist — the S3\nbuckets synced nothing, so /labs/federation/ 403''d in prod.","tree":{"sha":"fb7b44859c40c01836d34616d8d6d0798fdee5d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/trees/fb7b44859c40c01836d34616d8d6d0798fdee5d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/commits/1d832a783bb44e2e42fa21fd8dc82a590fa6846c","verification":{"payload":"tree fb7b44859c40c01836d34616d8d6d0798fdee5d4\nparent d543a43c5ebfa0130122bb45b5aaeff7ebee16f4\nauthor André Gomes <andregs@users.noreply.github.com> 1783134068 -0300\ncommitter André Gomes <andregs@users.noreply.github.com> 1783134068 -0300\n\nfix(federation): build to app-local dist, not repo-root dist/apps\n\noutDir pointed at ../../dist/apps/federation-* (repo root) while\ninfra''s createSyncedFolder reads apps/federation-*/dist — the S3\nbuckets synced nothing, so /labs/federation/ 403''d in prod.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoNX1QTsJGc/NYn+qL8qTQcygP0\n90pA84L/ce+2vjPvgAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDPA/pHwa3Gpz8iljdzXseTj8EjlQySk/2AxAyfBCXaUXQe4qKO9HzZ6WMVp6UHoGD\nKq94UyUF7oGUPZzpMzZwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-04T03:01:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/712092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andregs","id":712092,"login":"andregs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjA5Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/andregs/lean-dev-br/commit/1d832a783bb44e2e42fa21fd8dc82a590fa6846c","node_id":"C_kwDOSwhTatoAKDFkODMyYTc4M2JiNDRlMmU0MmZhMjFmZDhkYzgyYTU5MGZhNjg0NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/andregs/lean-dev-br/commit/d543a43c5ebfa0130122bb45b5aaeff7ebee16f4","sha":"d543a43c5ebfa0130122bb45b5aaeff7ebee16f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/d543a43c5ebfa0130122bb45b5aaeff7ebee16f4"}],"sha":"1d832a783bb44e2e42fa21fd8dc82a590fa6846c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/1d832a783bb44e2e42fa21fd8dc82a590fa6846c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/712092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andregs","id":712092,"login":"andregs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjA5Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andregs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/commits/d543a43c5ebfa0130122bb45b5aaeff7ebee16f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-04T02:37:54Z","email":"andregs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"André Gomes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-04T02:37:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(federation): Module Federation twin of ui-modulith Labs demo (#31)\n\n* feat(federation): add kernel lib for Labs microfrontend demo\n\nEventBus + BusProvider/useBus + openapi-fetch client, mirroring\nlibs/ui-modulith/kernel. Consumed as a shared MF2 singleton across\nthe shell and remotes so the bus instance survives the remote boundary.\n\n* feat(federation): scaffold federation-catalog remote app skeleton\n\nReact+Vite app via @nx/react, port 4204, base /labs/federation/catalog/.\nBare skeleton for now — Module Federation wiring and real catalog\nfeature content land in follow-up commits.\n\n* feat(federation): scaffold federation-cart remote app skeleton\n\nReact+Vite app via @nx/react, port 4205, base /labs/federation/cart/.\nBare skeleton for now — Module Federation wiring and real cart\nfeature content land in follow-up commits.\n\n* feat(federation): scaffold federation-shell host app skeleton\n\nReact+Vite app via @nx/react, port 4203, base /labs/federation/.\nBare skeleton for now — Module Federation host wiring, MSW, BusProvider\nand routing land in follow-up commits.\n\n* feat(federation): expose catalog and cart as MF2 remotes\n\nAdd @module-federation/vite federation() config to both apps, exposing\na placeholder ./Routes and sharing react/react-dom/react-router-dom/\nfederation-kernel as singletons. dts generation disabled — its default\noutput path collides with ESLint''s typed-linting project service.\nbuild.target: chrome89 avoids esbuild needing to downlevel the MF2\nruntime''s top-level-await chunks.\n\nReal catalog/cart feature content lands in follow-up commits, wired\ninto the shell next.\n\n* feat(federation): wire shell as MF2 host, consume catalog+cart remotes\n\nfederation() host config with dev/prod-aware remote entry URLs (each\nremote is its own dev server locally, same-origin under CloudFront\nin prod). app.tsx wraps BusProvider + BrowserRouter around routes\nthat lazy-load catalog/Routes and cart/Routes.\n\nVerified end-to-end with live dev servers on all three apps: shell\nloads both federated remotes with zero console errors, / redirects\nto /catalog, /cart resolves independently.\n\nDropped app.tsx''s unit test — it lazy-loads remotes over the network,\nwhich vitest/jsdom can''t resolve; same precedent as ui-modulith,\nwhich only unit-tests components with real logic (DemoBar), not its\nown thin app.tsx/routes.tsx. Covered by e2e instead.\n\n* fix(federation): enable cross-remote dts with ambient fallback for cold builds\n\ndts:true generates real types for catalog/Routes and cart/Routes, but\nonly when the remote''s dev server is live — consumeTypes always fetches\nover HTTP (node-fetch), with no local-file fallback even for file://\nURLs (confirmed via FEDERATION_DEBUG). Explored generateTypes.outputDir\n+ consumeTypes.remoteTypeUrls + typesOnBuild per the official docs;\nnone make it work cold. Making it work would mean standing up throwaway\nHTTP servers around the build — not worth it for 2 exposed modules.\n\ntsconfig paths map catalog/Routes and cart/Routes to the real generated\n@mf-types/ output; federation-remotes.d.ts is the ambient fallback used\nonly when that file is absent (cold build/CI). Both coexist without\nconflict — TS always prefers the real file when present.\n\nAlso: gitignore/eslint-ignore/vscode-exclude the generated @mf-types\nand dummy-non-existing-folder dirs (the latter a Vitest 4 + Vite 8\nregression, https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/10617 — Vitest''s\nsentinel build.outDir gets physically created instead of staying\nvirtual); include eslint.config.mjs in the root tsconfig so\nimport.meta.dirname resolves against @types/node.\n\n* feat(federation): build real catalog feature content\n\nCatalogPage grid + ProductDetail, ported from libs/ui-modulith/catalog\nwith kernel import paths swapped. Shares react-i18next/i18next as MF2\nsingletons (missed in the earlier remote-exposal commit). Standalone\nentry (nx serve federation-catalog alone) is now a lightweight dev\nplaceholder, not a full harness — real providers come from the shell.\n\nTwo dts fixes found while getting a clean build:\n- dts.tsConfigPath defaults to tsconfig.json (no include), not\n  tsconfig.app.json — its isolated compile couldn''t resolve CSS-module\n  ambient types. Set explicitly.\n- extractThirdParty writes sibling .d.ts files directly into\n  federation-kernel''s src/ tree whenever an app pulls it in as shared.\n  Ignored in kernel''s own eslint config (schema.d.ts is the one real\n  exception) and via .gitignore.\n\nVisually compared against ui-modulith through the shell: catalog''s own\nCSS module renders correctly and is byte-identical to the modulith\ntwin, but the shell has no design-system CSS/SiteNav/SiteFooter yet —\nthat''s the next commit.\n\n* feat(federation): build real cart feature content\n\nCartPage + useCartLines reducer, ported from libs/ui-modulith/cart with\nkernel import paths swapped. Pure bus consumer, no API — replay-on-\nsubscribe is what reconstructs the cart when this remote mounts after\ncatalog already emitted cart/add events, same as the modulith twin but\nnow crossing an actual remote boundary instead of a lazy import.\n\nApplied the same two dts fixes proactively (tsConfigPath + i18n/\nreact-i18next shared singletons) since they''re now known necessary for\nevery remote — verified clean build (no TYPE-001) on the first try.\n\n* feat(federation): wire shell page chrome and fix i18n singleton sharing\n\ndesign-system CSS (tokens/base/nav/footer), SiteNav/SiteFooter, i18n\ninit, and DemoBar (cart-count badge), ported from ui-modulith''s\napp.tsx/app.css/DemoBar with kernel import paths swapped.\n\nFound and fixed a real bug while visually comparing against\nui-modulith: i18next/react-i18next were declared as MF2 shared\nsingletons in catalog and cart''s vite config, but never in the\nshell''s — the host never registered itself into the shared scope for\nthose packages, so catalog''s useTranslation always fell through to\n\"NO_I18NEXT_INSTANCE\". Added the same shared entries to the shell.\n\nVerified end-to-end via Playwright with live dev servers: catalog and\ncart both render fully translated (no raw i18n keys), and a product\nadded in the catalog remote correctly appears in the cart remote via\nthe kernel EventBus — crossing two separate remote boundaries, not\njust one. Catalog''s screenshot is now pixel-identical to ui-modulith''s\nequivalent page.\n\n* feat(federation): wire MSW as the shell''s permanent mock backend\n\nPorted from ui-modulith/src/mocks with kernel import + base URL\nswapped (/labs/federation/api). Lives in the shell only — service\nworkers intercept at the page/origin level, so catalog and cart''s own\napiClient calls get caught too regardless of which remote made them.\n\nVerified end-to-end with live dev servers: catalog grid shows all 3\nreal MSW-backed products, product detail page resolves by SKU, zero\nconsole errors. Demo is now fully self-contained, no route mocking\nneeded for manual testing.\n\n* feat(federation): wire CSP and Trusted Types across all three apps\n\nAdded ''federation'' to the shared CSP lib (same MSW/no-reCAPTCHA\nprofile as ui-modulith, plus a dev-only script-src relaxation for the\nshell to load catalog/cart''s remoteEntry.js from their own cross-origin\ndev servers — same-origin in prod, so this stays dev-only). Wired\ncspHeader into all three apps'' dev+preview headers; ported\ntrusted-types.ts to the shell (same MSW service-worker script-URL sink,\nnow also covering MF2''s dynamic remoteEntry/chunk script tags — both\nsame-origin under /labs/federation/ in production).\n\nVerified with vite preview (real prod build + enforced CSP): the\nserved header has no localhost leak and enforces Trusted Types\ncorrectly; the MSW service worker registers and activates cleanly\nunder enforcement, with zero CSP or TT violations in the console.\n\n* feat(homepage): enable labs-federation flag\n\nSame pattern as labs-modulith: flag + gated card + locale keys (en-US\nand pt-BR, parity-checked). Verified rendered card links to\n/labs/federation/ with correctly translated copy in both locales.\n\n* feat(infra): add 3-bucket S3 + CloudFront topology for the federation lab\n\nfederation-shell, federation-catalog, federation-cart each get their\nown bucket/OAC/response-headers-policy/bucket-policy/synced-folder,\nmirroring the existing per-app pattern (blog, todo, ui-modulith).\nCatalog/cart''s cache behaviors and edge-fn prefix-stripping are ordered\nbefore the shell''s broader /labs/federation/* catch-all, since both\ntheir paths also start with that prefix.\n\nVerified via `pulumi preview` against the real prod stack: 21 new\nfederation-specific resources (additive only), and the shared\nCloudFront distribution + edge function both get safe in-place\nupdates (diff: origins/orderedCacheBehaviors, code) — no replacement\nof shared infrastructure, no impact to existing routes.\n\n* fix(federation): scope remote routing to actual asset files, not the whole prefix\n\nThe original CloudFront cache behaviors and edge-fn stripping routed\nALL of /labs/federation/catalog/* and /cart/* to those remotes''\nbuckets. Caught by testing the real same-origin topology locally (via\na new preview.proxy on the shell): a direct navigation/refresh at\n/labs/federation/catalog rendered catalog''s own standalone placeholder\ninstead of the shell''s routed CatalogPage, since catalog and cart are\nthe shell''s own internal SPA routes, not separate apps like\nui-modulith — unlike ui-modulith''s /catalog and /cart, they must\nnever redirect or route to another bucket.\n\nFixed by narrowing both the CloudFront cache behaviors and the edge\nfunction to only catalog/cart''s real asset files (assets/*, the exact\nremoteEntry.js) — everything else, including a bare /catalog\nnavigation, now correctly falls through to the shell''s catch-all.\n\nVerified via Playwright against the real 3-preview-server same-origin\nsetup: full catalog → add to cart → cart flow works, and a direct\nnavigation to /catalog renders the shell''s page, not the remote''s\nplaceholder.\n\n* test(federation): add federation-shell-e2e Playwright suite\n\nMirrors ui-modulith-e2e/add-to-cart.spec.ts, adapted for three\nseparate preview servers (shell + catalog + cart) instead of one —\nPlaywright''s webServer array starts all three; the shell''s preview\nproxy makes them same-origin, matching the real CloudFront topology.\n\nAdds a fifth test beyond the modulith twin: a direct navigation to\n/catalog must render the shell''s routed page, not catalog''s own\nstandalone entry — the regression test for the routing bug fixed in\nthe previous commit.\n\nAll 5 tests pass against the real 3-server setup with enforced\nproduction CSP.\n\n* ci(federation): wire federation apps into the deploy pipeline\n\nAdd federation-shell/-catalog/-cart to the affected-projects filter\nthat decides whether to run deploy-frontend, and to the explicit\nbuild -p list (Nx''s own project graph doesn''t see the host↔remote\nrelationship — it''s just string URLs in vite config, not real\nimports — so this can''t be inferred the way ui-modulith''s own build\nalready is).\n\nci.yml (PR verify) needed no changes — it''s driven entirely by\n`nx affected`, which already covers every new Nx project including\nfederation-shell-e2e.\n\n* docs(federation): add modulith-vs-federation comparison with measured data\n\nReal network waterfall (58 req/622KB vs 8 req/263KB), isolated build\ntimings, and cited HTTP/2 stream-limit research, plus the three\nfootguns hit building the twin.","tree":{"sha":"5c153725843a8de405a449972c28b85c5bbd3b8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/trees/5c153725843a8de405a449972c28b85c5bbd3b8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andregs/lean-dev-br/git/commits/d543a43c5ebfa0130122bb45b5aaeff7ebee16f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c153725843a8de405a449972c28b85c5bbd3b8c\nparent 1378718d20c0f0875e2cb21b2ed3ab09ddf1efd8\nauthor André Gomes <andregs@users.noreply.github.com> 1783132674 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783132674 -0300\n\nfeat(federation): Module Federation twin of ui-modulith Labs demo (#31)\n\n* feat(federation): add kernel lib for Labs microfrontend demo\n\nEventBus + BusProvider/useBus + openapi-fetch client, mirroring\nlibs/ui-modulith/kernel. Consumed as a shared MF2 singleton across\nthe shell and remotes so the bus instance survives the remote boundary.\n\n* feat(federation): scaffold federation-catalog remote app skeleton\n\nReact+Vite app via @nx/react, port 4204, base /labs/federation/catalog/.\nBare skeleton for now — Module Federation wiring and real catalog\nfeature content land in follow-up commits.\n\n* feat(federation): scaffold federation-cart remote app skeleton\n\nReact+Vite app via @nx/react, port 4205, base /labs/federation/cart/.\nBare skeleton for now — Module Federation wiring and real cart\nfeature content land in follow-up commits.\n\n* feat(federation): scaffold federation-shell host app skeleton\n\nReact+Vite app via @nx/react, port 4203, base /labs/federation/.\nBare skeleton for now — Module Federation host wiring, MSW, BusProvider\nand routing land in follow-up commits.\n\n* feat(federation): expose catalog and cart as MF2 remotes\n\nAdd @module-federation/vite federation() config to both apps, exposing\na placeholder ./Routes and sharing react/react-dom/react-router-dom/\nfederation-kernel as singletons. dts generation disabled — its default\noutput path collides with ESLint''s typed-linting project service.\nbuild.target: chrome89 avoids esbuild needing to downlevel the MF2\nruntime''s top-level-await chunks.\n\nReal catalog/cart feature content lands in follow-up commits, wired\ninto the shell next.\n\n* feat(federation): wire shell as MF2 host, consume catalog+cart remotes\n\nfederation() host config with dev/prod-aware remote entry URLs (each\nremote is its own dev server locally, same-origin under CloudFront\nin prod). app.tsx wraps BusProvider + BrowserRouter around routes\nthat lazy-load catalog/Routes and cart/Routes.\n\nVerified end-to-end with live dev servers on all three apps: shell\nloads both federated remotes with zero console errors, / redirects\nto /catalog, /cart resolves independently.\n\nDropped app.tsx''s unit test — it lazy-loads remotes over the network,\nwhich vitest/jsdom can''t resolve; same precedent as ui-modulith,\nwhich only unit-tests components with real logic (DemoBar), not its\nown thin app.tsx/routes.tsx. Covered by e2e instead.\n\n* fix(federation): enable cross-remote dts with ambient fallback for cold builds\n\ndts:true generates real types for catalog/Routes and cart/Routes, but\nonly when the remote''s dev server is live — consumeTypes always fetches\nover HTTP (node-fetch), with no local-file fallback even for file://\nURLs (confirmed via FEDERATION_DEBUG). Explored generateTypes.outputDir\n+ consumeTypes.remoteTypeUrls + typesOnBuild per the official docs;\nnone make it work cold. Making it work would mean standing up throwaway\nHTTP servers around the build — not worth it for 2 exposed modules.\n\ntsconfig paths map catalog/Routes and cart/Routes to the real generated\n@mf-types/ output; federation-remotes.d.ts is the ambient fallback used\nonly when that file is absent (cold build/CI). Both coexist without\nconflict — TS always prefers the real file when present.\n\nAlso: gitignore/eslint-ignore/vscode-exclude the generated @mf-types\nand dummy-non-existing-folder dirs (the latter a Vitest 4 + Vite 8\nregression, https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/10617 — Vitest''s\nsentinel build.outDir gets physically created instead of staying\nvirtual); include eslint.config.mjs in the root tsconfig so\nimport.meta.dirname resolves against @types/node.\n\n* feat(federation): build real catalog feature content\n\nCatalogPage grid + ProductDetail, ported from libs/ui-modulith/catalog\nwith kernel import paths swapped. Shares react-i18next/i18next as MF2\nsingletons (missed in the earlier remote-exposal commit). Standalone\nentry (nx serve federation-catalog alone) is now a lightweight dev\nplaceholder, not a full harness — real providers come from the shell.\n\nTwo dts fixes found while getting a clean build:\n- dts.tsConfigPath defaults to tsconfig.json (no include), not\n  tsconfig.app.json — its isolated compile couldn''t resolve CSS-module\n  ambient types. Set explicitly.\n- extractThirdParty writes sibling .d.ts files directly into\n  federation-kernel''s src/ tree whenever an app pulls it in as shared.\n  Ignored in kernel''s own eslint config (schema.d.ts is the one real\n  exception) and via .gitignore.\n\nVisually compared against ui-modulith through the shell: catalog''s own\nCSS module renders correctly and is byte-identical to the modulith\ntwin, but the shell has no design-system CSS/SiteNav/SiteFooter yet —\nthat''s the next commit.\n\n* feat(federation): build real cart feature content\n\nCartPage + useCartLines reducer, ported from libs/ui-modulith/cart with\nkernel import paths swapped. Pure bus consumer, no API — replay-on-\nsubscribe is what reconstructs the cart when this remote mounts after\ncatalog already emitted cart/add events, same as the modulith twin but\nnow crossing an actual remote boundary instead of a lazy import.\n\nApplied the same two dts fixes proactively (tsConfigPath + i18n/\nreact-i18next shared singletons) since they''re now known necessary for\nevery remote — verified clean build (no TYPE-001) on the first try.\n\n* feat(federation): wire shell page chrome and fix i18n singleton sharing\n\ndesign-system CSS (tokens/base/nav/footer), SiteNav/SiteFooter, i18n\ninit, and DemoBar (cart-count badge), ported from ui-modulith''s\napp.tsx/app.css/DemoBar with kernel import paths swapped.\n\nFound and fixed a real bug while visually comparing against\nui-modulith: i18next/react-i18next were declared as MF2 shared\nsingletons in catalog and cart''s vite config, but never in the\nshell''s — the host never registered itself into the shared scope for\nthose packages, so catalog''s useTranslation always fell through to\n\"NO_I18NEXT_INSTANCE\". Added the same shared entries to the shell.\n\nVerified end-to-end via Playwright with live dev servers: catalog and\ncart both render fully translated (no raw i18n keys), and a product\nadded in the catalog remote correctly appears in the cart remote via\nthe kernel EventBus — crossing two separate remote boundaries, not\njust one. Catalog''s screenshot is now pixel-identical to ui-modulith''s\nequivalent page.\n\n* feat(federation): wire MSW as the shell''s permanent mock backend\n\nPorted from ui-modulith/src/mocks with kernel import + base URL\nswapped (/labs/federation/api). Lives in the shell only — service\nworkers intercept at the page/origin level, so catalog and cart''s own\napiClient calls get caught too regardless of which remote made them.\n\nVerified end-to-end with live dev servers: catalog grid shows all 3\nreal MSW-backed products, product detail page resolves by SKU, zero\nconsole errors. Demo is now fully self-contained, no route mocking\nneeded for manual testing.\n\n* feat(federation): wire CSP and Trusted Types across all three apps\n\nAdded ''federation'' to the shared CSP lib (same MSW/no-reCAPTCHA\nprofile as ui-modulith, plus a dev-only script-src relaxation for the\nshell to load catalog/cart''s remoteEntry.js from their own cross-origin\ndev servers — same-origin in prod, so this stays dev-only). Wired\ncspHeader into all three apps'' dev+preview headers; ported\ntrusted-types.ts to the shell (same MSW service-worker script-URL sink,\nnow also covering MF2''s dynamic remoteEntry/chunk script tags — both\nsame-origin under /labs/federation/ in production).\n\nVerified with vite preview (real prod build + enforced CSP): the\nserved header has no localhost leak and enforces Trusted Types\ncorrectly; the MSW service worker registers and activates cleanly\nunder enforcement, with zero CSP or TT violations in the console.\n\n* feat(homepage): enable labs-federation flag\n\nSame pattern as labs-modulith: flag + gated card + locale keys (en-US\nand pt-BR, parity-checked). Verified rendered card links to\n/labs/federation/ with correctly translated copy in both locales.\n\n* feat(infra): add 3-bucket S3 + CloudFront topology for the federation lab\n\nfederation-shell, federation-catalog, federation-cart each get their\nown bucket/OAC/response-headers-policy/bucket-policy/synced-folder,\nmirroring the existing per-app pattern (blog, todo, ui-modulith).\nCatalog/cart''s cache behaviors and edge-fn prefix-stripping are ordered\nbefore the shell''s broader /labs/federation/* catch-all, since both\ntheir paths also start with that prefix.\n\nVerified via `pulumi preview` against the real prod stack: 21 new\nfederation-specific resources (additive only), and the shared\nCloudFront distribution + edge function both get safe in-place\nupdates (diff: origins/orderedCacheBehaviors, code) — no replacement\nof shared infrastructure, no impact to existing routes.\n\n* fix(federation): scope remote routing to actual asset files, not the whole prefix\n\nThe original CloudFront cache behaviors and edge-fn stripping routed\nALL of /labs/federation/catalog/* and /cart/* to those remotes''\nbuckets. Caught by testing the real same-origin topology locally (via\na new preview.proxy on the shell): a direct navigation/refresh at\n/labs/federation/catalog rendered catalog''s own standalone placeholder\ninstead of the shell''s routed CatalogPage, since catalog and cart are\nthe shell''s own internal SPA routes, not separate apps like\nui-modulith — unlike ui-modulith''s /catalog and /cart, they must\nnever redirect or route to another bucket.\n\nFixed by narrowing both the CloudFront cache behaviors and the edge\nfunction to only catalog/cart''s real asset files (assets/*, the exact\nremoteEntry.js) — everything else, including a bare /catalog\nnavigation, now correctly falls through to the shell''s catch-all.\n\nVerified via Playwright against the real 3-preview-server same-origin\nsetup: full catalog → add to cart → cart flow works, and a direct\nnavigation to /catalog renders the shell''s page, not the remote''s\nplaceholder.\n\n* test(federation): add federation-shell-e2e Playwright suite\n\nMirrors ui-modulith-e2e/add-to-cart.spec.ts, adapted for three\nseparate preview servers (shell + catalog + cart) instead of one —\nPlaywright''s webServer array starts all three; the shell''s preview\nproxy makes them same-origin, matching the real CloudFront topology.\n\nAdds a fifth test beyond the modulith twin: a direct navigation to\n/catalog must render the shell''s routed page, not catalog''s own\nstandalone entry — the regression test for the routing bug fixed in\nthe previous commit.\n\nAll 5 tests pass against the real 3-server setup with enforced\nproduction CSP.\n\n* ci(federation): wire federation apps into the deploy pipeline\n\nAdd federation-shell/-catalog/-cart to the affected-projects filter\nthat decides whether to run deploy-frontend, and to the explicit\nbuild -p list (Nx''s own project graph doesn''t see the host↔remote\nrelationship — it''s just string URLs in vite config, not real\nimports — so this can''t be inferred the way ui-modulith''s own build\nalready is).\n\nci.yml (PR verify) needed no changes — it''s driven entirely by\n`nx affected`, which already covers every new Nx project including\nfederation-shell-e2e.\n\n* docs(federation): add modulith-vs-federation comparison with measured data\n\nReal network waterfall (58 req/622KB vs 8 req/263KB), isolated build\ntimings, and cited HTTP/2 stream-limit research, plus the three\nfootguns hit building the twin.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSHIDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjo4QAJ1rGLBm4oVR+kbkeYwJk11y\nspFHkazefNe9yG0ubWUFAk8fVyXDizIbYkQIvd0Lqv8icdND2WTN20+S+kYHjVBq\nTTOc6g9NGsa0NL5mNSRFOBl4zVX8pf21o1PUWXqrlnGpvL5lPxR3lGi4TurelfcT\n1dXkIYEdS14i/a3aMxntadnTSsIH2clTc/Jegkqfbnsxm1PZrnHD1W0J6PSJ69Na\n+ZJuh4HO8gV/xuSrqrGhpagwQ0icgnmyz+whWnBqnBt1a6GlL7VW/DRXubyNc4bh\njc2FK3WFutjUTLz/fG5QXOQ+kc6G1NiC4A0omJQ0unm1oTYIz1kCV6NtMnSW385o\nteCW8Byjuq2vZXIRv31hUI8hc3t7JIkr2R6AM6zE4Ad7E29rXOAF9PEqINodz95z\nB53QIAEecWBUvxMAe+ce6YqwHBzm3ErWehqaD/6gbx4EzXLfD6XP2eScbbESUXXr\nbZVytMl5MzZ7BL5fa1CMpZDuaMwPPcDHQsPaCnPVhAfekyH0kCjelzC7lwcGdwl8\nwpwa3JtHbt4QoJmRzU3vOmdRK/uTc/ZCW6EoutMufwrqW1CN+Hj2sNBCeOoDsmr+\nDWMsBW1sW2b7639edfwJtZULbE0cvyauHmMvyG0zG6utOQd892nn2GulCNfCSDIJ\nWrOasr/ATG/io2yx4vkm\n=dyJ1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-04T02:37:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u